### F.2 A11 / C8 — "a stamp renewed four times" → OWNER; default wording to carry

**The count after B5 M9.** On paper at B6's entry: the Greyvane grant and **two** renewals — the twentieth of Reaping (B4; B5 ch1:125 "one semester stamp, renewed") and the mill town (B5 M2). The half-year sitting that the cadence put at Norhold did not sit (M9 ruling; author note (j)); the next by cadence falls about the first term's close in B6 (M5), not in the interval. So the applied PENDING notes (BM:22, BM:584, SL:30, M1:35 item 10), which said "at most three", are now "two", and nothing in B5 can supply the pole's "four".

**Default to carry until the owner rules** (the protected line BM:584 stays verbatim; every non-protected count tells the truth; no sentence other than the pole states a number):
- `BM:22` old `Greyvane precedent, four semester panels renewed, Magister Gault evaluator of record. [PENDING B5 M9 — audit A11/C8: … "four" is held, unchanged, until B5 M9 closes.]` → new `Greyvane precedent, the stamp and its two renewals on paper (the twentieth of Reaping; the mill town — the half-year sitting that fell at Norhold did not sit, B5 M9 ruling), Magister Gault evaluator of record. [B5-reconciled 2026-10-06: B5 M9 closed with no Norhold session (C8); OWNER-pending #42: the protected first pole's "a stamp renewed four times" (§8) — audit §F A11]`
- `SL:30` old `four panel renewals [PENDING B5 M9 — audit A11/C8: … held, unchanged]` → new `the stamp and its two renewals on paper — the twentieth of Reaping and the mill town; no sitting sat at Norhold (B5 M9 ruling) [B5-reconciled 2026-10-06: OWNER-pending #42 for the protected pole's "four"; audit §F A11]`
- `M1:35` item (10) old `The stamp and its renewals: [PENDING B5 M9 — audit A11/C8]; at most three on paper, so the first-pole entry's "four" is held, unchanged, for now.` → new `The stamp and its renewals: two on paper (the twentieth of Reaping; the mill town); no sitting sat at Norhold (B5 M9). The protected first-pole entry keeps "a stamp renewed four times" verbatim (OWNER-pending #42); no other sentence in M1 states a count of renewals, and M1 stages no sitting in the interval unless the owner chooses option (c) below.`
- `BM:584` old `[PENDING B5 M9 — audit A11/C8: … OWNER item; no wording changed.]` → new `[OWNER-pending #42 (audit §F A11): B5 M9 closed with no Norhold session, so the file carries the Greyvane grant and TWO renewals (the twentieth of Reaping; the mill town). Options: (a) accept Cael's rounding — the four impressions on his sheet are the grant, the two renewals and the tournament office's filing stamp (B5 T3), though the pole's own list already counts "a tournament their own clause put me in" separately, so this reading strains; (b) amend the protected line to "a stamp renewed twice" or "a stamp and its renewals" — the honest reading, one word, touches protected text; (c) stage the displaced half-year sitting in M1's interval log in one clause ("the sitting the tournament displaced was taken the week they got home") — three renewals, still one short without (a). Coordinator default until ruled: the line stands verbatim and nothing else on the page counts. No wording changed.]`

Recommendation to the owner: (b). It costs one word of protected text and leaves no arithmetic for a reader to do.

### F.3 The four option choices — confirmed, with evidence

1. **B3 (the confluence meet; a lighter card in a non-qualifying year; Lira's Silver bout as a cross-tier host-exhibition filing). CONFIRMED.** The host-option mechanism is #39's and B5's practice (Cael's exhibitions under the demonstration provision at every meet; the Iron split as a host option, ch10–12). One correction of the APPLIED note's reasoning (§5.1 / §2 B3): B5's confluence is not "after the cache" in B6's order — in B5 it sat at d107–109, about five weeks BEFORE the cold term (d119; whole-arc read §1), i.e. at the first term's close in B6's shape, which is M5, not M6. So the gap between B6's M4 slot ("the first term's middle to late weeks") and B5's slot is a few weeks, not a season, and the "lighter, earlier card" line is a harmless default rather than a necessity. The owner may instead keep the meet at B5's slot by letting it fall at the first term's close; nothing else moves. B5's confluence venue is the river guild's new hall and the salt store (B5 STATE_LEDGER:813); B6's "four facts" floor is B6's own. No plan change.
2. **B9 ("the summer qualification" → the registry's Silver advancement evaluation that Rooke's program builds toward, falling after the ruling). CONFIRMED.** B5's vocabulary supports it exactly: ranks and tiers change only at sittings and by advancement evaluation ("gone up to Rank Eight at the year's last sitting", ch21:63; "advanced at the last sitting before the year's turn", ch20:231; Brom's "Mandatory advancement review … They'll look me over for Iron", ch60:145); the move to the Silver bracket is by rating at such an evaluation, not by the three-year qualifying season (ch60:71 "They'll be in the Silver bracket next time"). Use B5's words on the page — "advancement evaluation", "the sitting" — and never "qualification" for it. No plan change.
3. **C7 (the senior third-year Rank Seven, advanced at the last sitting; Ephram stays Six). CONFIRMED, one gloss corrected.** "Advanced at the year's last sitting" is B5's phrase (ch20:231, ch21:63). But the applied gloss at `BM:179` — "Ephram stays Rank Six, the top of the Iron column in B4 ch8" — conflates two things the edition keeps apart: the registry rank (Iron Rank Six) and the Crown yard's Iron column, which is the hill's results board ("His name had stood at the head of the Iron column in the Crown yard for two years; by the only measure the hill used, he was the best fighter on it", ch1:211; ch8:259 "nobody looks at the top of a column"). In the edition a Rank Seven outranks a Rank Six on paper (see F.5), and that is fine: the column stays Ephram's by results.
   - `BM:179` old `Ephram stays Rank Six, the top of the Iron column in B4 ch8; audit C7]` → new `Ephram stays Iron Rank Six and keeps the head of the Crown yard's Iron column — the hill's results board, not a rank (B5 ch1:211, ch8:259); a Rank Seven on paper does not move him off it; audit C7, §F.3]`
4. **B2 (Lira vs the Silver R8: "two touches to one on the fourth exchange"; the author sets which exchanges score). CONFIRMED, with the order fixed by the beat list.** Under #39's exhibition format (five at most; two touches ends it) the beats at `M4:23` / `BM:226` — "lose the first … take the centre; outbuilt in the third; half a stride short in the fourth" — can only score as: E1 touch to the R8; E2 touch to Lira; E3 no touch (outbuilt, nothing lands); E4 touch to the R8, which ends it, two to one on the fourth exchange. If E3 scored, the bout would end there. One texture note: "going away into the ropes" is the source's; B5's regional floors have walls, barriers and pillar corners (the mill hall's "north rope" is the one roped floor, ch11:89) — the author may keep ropes if the confluence floor is given them once.
   - `M4:23` after `the result is two touches to one on the fourth exchange, not "three to one"; audit B2, B3]` insert ` [B5-reconciled 2026-10-06: the touches fall E1 (his), E2 (hers), E4 (his); E3 is clean, or the bout ends in three under #39; audit §F.3]`

