editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:222:**Injuries tracked forward (no silent healing):** Cael's calf (53 → reopened 78 and 96 → closed 99); ribs (78 → taped 81 → off 99 → the Hall's bill 119 → cold-aggravated 123 → quiet at 129). Lira's right ankle (53, 78, 96; **never mended**); her leg (broken 78, mended 80); her left forearm (96 → season order → reopened 114 → closed; slung at 131). Brom's forearm (53 → reopened 78 → mended 80); his hand (96 → mended 97); his shoulder (114 → mended; reopened 119 → mended twice → bound 120). Karis's palms (53, scars); empty (78); throat and voice (96 → mended 97, voice back by ~110). Seln: unmarked. Oryn: drained at every mending, priced aloud.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:240:Callbacks confirmed in Book 8's closed prose: Oryn's letter and "Find me at Thornwater." / "Bring the map." (B8 Ch1, Ch24); "a tape and a season" (B8 Ch1); "Lie still when I say" (B8 Ch18, Ch24); Brom's "Twice… not three times this season" (B8 Ch6); "A measurement is a fact about a ruler, not about the hand that held it." (B8 Ch1, Ch5, Ch20); Hesk's "true to a hair" / "draw a line through it" / "Mind the shape" (B8 Ch1, Ch17, Ch18, Ch22, Ch24); "too small" (B8 Ch16, Ch17, Ch24); "Stop touching it." (B8 Ch7); "Not the Quiet." (B8 Ch7, Ch24); "He'll speak to you when you've cost him something" (B8 Ch7); Teague's spring term (B8 Ch1, Ch17); "Eleventh" (B8 Ch1, Ch12, Ch17); "the Bronze from Ardenmere" (B8 Ch7); ninety-six in hand (B8 Ch1); fifty-two sheets and forty-one kinds (B8 Ch9–11). Canon documents quote "Three points make a line. Four make an argument.", "Someone made this pattern.", the looms finding, "A circle is a made shape." and the stratum limit. Every other item below is a signature line or document of this book. **Keep them all exact.** Speaker attributions may be re-staged; the words may not.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:259:- Pike's season line (Ch24): "*Crew of six. Ford cleared, traverse mapped, Ring entered, Stair entered and instruments recovered, Hall entered. No losses. Returned every time.*" — and the Stair's price column: *three hundred; taken; not paid*.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:269:- **Oryn's letter (Ch24):** *Route's whole. The knee held. Nobody died of three weeks. Spring: bring the map, and lie still when I say. — O.* — then: Six, by letter. (The architecture and series docs still quote "eleven days"; prose and Book 8 say **three weeks**. See C6.)
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:272:- Ch1 close: *Note the date. Season's open, and for once it isn't theirs.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:284:- Ch14, the birthday line: *Hundred and second day past the Line. Nineteen. Written at Thornwater, in the steading's common room, autumn, the fire lit for us. Witnesses: four of my own, and a healer who's a stop.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:304:- Ch7: Oryn: "That's a tape and a season. It'll set." — "Twenty days," … "Round. Two at a hold, near enough, and the road between, and the road's the part that doesn't move." — "I remember who I've had my hands on," … "That's the book. A healer who needs a page to know who's owed has stopped looking at them." — "In the city I healed Bronzes with bruises. Out here I set legs. I'm not going back and I'm not stopping. The route is the only thing I own." — "It's like putting my hands in a river in the dark. Something's moving. I can't find the banks, so I can't read it, so I can't touch it. That's the rule. I didn't make it." — "When you're not broken, I run the long one. It won't read you either. I want to feel it not read you properly." — "Thornwater's on my route in nine days. You'll be on the board by then. Come find me. I want to read you when you're not broken." / "Nine days." — The ford-keeper: "Then they go round," … "That's worth seventy to know before the first cart's in the gorge. I'd sooner pay it for this." — Teague: "You cleared Thornwater's ford with five and lost a cart on the high bench with five." / "Yes." / "The ford was good work. The bench was a cart." … "The board's going to have you and me on the same contract inside a season. Be good enough that I'm glad."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:307:- Ch10: Karis: "Sixty-two cords and twenty strides," … "Twelve hundred and fifty-six meters, and a piece." … "A circle is a made shape." — Lira: "like a clock that stopped and started again without losing the time." — Seln: "You drive them where you've measured to. Not where you've measured from." … "Five years in the weather. A winter either side." — Brom: "Skin." — Karis: "It costs nothing. There's nothing to spend." — Seln: "I've a knife and fifteen years. It was never most of what I do." — Oryn: "Nothing. Not nothing in him. Nothing in my hands." … "A healer's hands stop working there." — Cael: "It was dark before," … "It's dark now." — Karis: "None I own. And I own more than the registry prints." — Seln: "They live in here because nothing that walks in can fight."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:308:- Ch11: Seln: "The road's cut." … "The grass. Where the cord went." — Oryn: "Move," … "I can't fix this here. Move." … "She keeps it." — **The order:** "A mend that deep holds nothing for a season. Nothing. That arm is not to hold. It's not to strike. It's not to catch. Not a rope, not a knife, not a fall, not a friend. Not until I say. And I'll say at first snow, near enough, if it's let alone." … "One arm. From here to the snow." — "The ankle's a tape and a season. I've told you that before." — Close: "It worked in there." / "Yours." / "Yes," Cael said. / "Later." / "Later."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:315:- Ch18: Oryn: "No." … "You asked. That's the rule and you kept it. The answer's no. Next." — "You're asking me to break the route," / "I'm not asking. I'm telling you where we'll be." / "That's worse. That's a healer's sentence." — "I'm not going to be anybody's sixth." — **Terms:** "You're on the route now. Which means when I say lie still, you lie still, and when I say I can't help you, you believe me." — "Well?" / "May I read you?" / "Yes. That's the answer, and I'm the one giving it…" — "You're built to arrive." / "Yes," she said. "That's what I am." — Lira: "He asked twice and got one," / Brom: "That's the rate," — Seln: "Newer. This one's been re-surveyed."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:316:- Ch19: Brom: "Ridge," — Seln: "They can shoot the bowl," … "They can't shoot the stair." — Oryn: "I can see what's wrong. I can't feel it and I can't touch it. Tape it. Leave the bolt." … "the bolt's the plug" … "I came south for exactly this. Enter that." — Oryn: "Ask first," — Lira: "Later." / "Later." — Oryn at the stone: "There. Back," … "The clock started again." — "It held a stair. It's not going to hold anything else this season." — Seln: "No faces." — Teague: "You walked out of the Quiet declaring," / "Yes." … "Then you're not on the board anymore. You're something the board doesn't have a column for."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:317:- Ch20: Teague: "We'll hold it till you're up." / "Noted" — Oryn: "What are they" / Karis: "Lines," — Karis: "He tried to drive it. Twice, by the head. It wouldn't go. Nothing goes into this." — Seln: "Nobody leaves a registry kit. It's signed out. You don't get another." … "I don't know what this is in, and I'm not going to say." — Karis: "Forty-one," … "every ten cords and a piece. Two hundred meters and a stride, to the stride." … "The floor was carved by somebody who knew the circle's size," … "A measurement is a fact about a ruler, not about the hand that held it."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:318:- Ch21: Oryn: "Big. Under. Comes up. Nobody's seen it whole." — Seln: "It's blind. It reads weight on the floor. It strikes where the weight is. And it strikes what *stays*." — Karis: "It reads that as the heaviest thing on the floor," / Cael: "It reads that as the thing that *stays*," — Lira: "We're going in without Paths to look at walls with a thing under the floor." / "Yes," Karis said. / "Just checking that's the plan." — Seln: "It's blind. It reads the floor. Get *off* the floor." — "You're copying," / "I'm not getting another chance," / "No, I can see that you're not," — *A thing that hunts what stays commits to the thing that stays hardest.* — "Brom," Cael said. "Wall. Your weight. Now." — Oryn: "Twice. It'll hold twice. It will not hold three times this season, so don't ask it to" — "You went in the water." / "You went in for Brom." / "Brom's on my route." … "So are you." … "Lie still. I want to read you."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:321:- Ch24: Pike: "Teague says you need a column I don't have. I've kept this ledger thirty years. First time it's been wrong about a crew by being too small." — the carters: "Eleventh," / "Aye," — Teague: "Spring. Whatever's on that bearing. My crew comes." / "Noted," — Pike: "Fence. Forty. Teague says it's yours if you want it; he's got the winter road," / Brom: "Ours," — Lira: "She'll say when," / Brom: "Spring," — *The sites were on an alignment. Not random.* — Karis: "Someone made this pattern." (said once; nobody answers) — **Closing, exact:** "I have ten things that aren't a Path," Cael said, eventually, to nobody in particular, "no tier, no rank, no file I can see — and five people, one of them on a route, who've walked into the quiet three times and come out." He turned it over once and let it stand. "And a line on a map that somebody drew before there was a registry to draw one." / Lira, one-armed, feeding the fire: "Then we follow it." / Brom: "Spring." / Karis, writing: "Noted." / Down the fire, the man who used to file reports about him watched the snow on the ferry landing with evident professional approval and said nothing, which — from him — was home. / Nothing out here had read him. At three floors older than any registry, every Path in the party had stopped at a line and his had not; a fourth had been paced from outside and not crossed. Nobody alive — least of all him — knew why. Someone had made the pattern. That was as far as anyone could say.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:327:| Reserved truth | This book may | This book may NOT |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:357:- **C8 · The Tide stall.** The bible (PROVISIONAL) defines a combat stall that Oryn "has done three times in her life." Neither Book 7 nor Book 8 shows it. **Recommend:** at most one mention, in Oryn's teaching in M3 as a limit she names and hates. Never used, since she is never made to fight. Owner may prefer omission.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:358:- **C9 · Lira's ankle.** The architecture checkpoint says the ankle was "mended once (Ch6)." The prose mended the tibia; the ankle is never mended in Book 7 ("a tape and a season"), and Book 8 Ch1 mends it. **Prose governs.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:360:- **C11 · Small counts.** Ch17 has Pike turning the ledger "which he had done once before" (it was twice: Ch2, Ch8). Ch24 has "twice in a season" (it is the fourth). Ch22 has "no captain eleven lines up" when Teague is ten up at eleventh. The retelling counts honestly. Convention: "N up" counts positions above; "N between" counts lines between.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:379:- Drafting may begin on the defaults. Ask the owner to rule on **C1** before Movement 1 is drafted, since it touches its opening chapters. C2, C3 and C8 can be ruled on before M3 and M6.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:381:- Book 8's DECISIONS file lists the facts Book 8 must not contradict. Every one is reproduced in this map's §1 ending, and none may move.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:27:- **Day 100, the deep reading (≈4,500):** the back room fixed from the door (window, table, stool, the roll in her order); "Breathe like a man asleep."; the count of ten ("Nothing. As before."); then the long one. The current goes *along*, not down; she can be felt keeping time; her commentary on banks (Iron Skin walled, Ember hot, Wind too fast to feel), "there's more water"; Shadow draws in under her touch; Storm quiet; he understands she is not afraid of him, because her trade has no room for being impressed; "Eleven years…". **The conditions arrive.** He could stop it, and stopping would be the lie. *He reached. Directed. Open-eyed. Still.* **The notice, exactly.** Two firsts counted; the third not written. "Something just changed…" / "No. I did. I need to tell you what I am." / "Then lie still while you do it…"
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:33:- "Compact" is said aloud **once** (Seln). Nothing about where the file is, what it says, or why. No dating past "five years… maybe six."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:23:- **The cascade: it listens, it doesn't pull (three nights).** His own current at the edge of every thought; the nine coming up out of it one at a time and told apart by sound; "a room he had lived in for eighteen years with the lights suddenly on." Brom on the ladder ("How many people." / "Nine. Ten. I can't hear the tenth. It's the thing I'm hearing with." / the forge story). Day two: **Storm heard resettling** in the yard, a hand on the well's rim; the ground arriving half a beat late under a counted foot, so he **relearns the Wind economy in the yard** while the listening runs (a learning encounter). **Oryn's "Where is it loudest."** "Here… It's not louder there. It's nearer." Ask first, said in the yard: "I ask the dying." / "I ask first. Every time."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:39:- Vastin: one window only, three sentences, no age. "Forty years" is his rounding.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:9:- POV: Cael ≈35,400. **Seln cutaway ≈2,200** (night of day 112, after the council: the two slips laid side by side in his head; six years carrying a case for people he cannot see; why he wants a face; he may not open the case or decode anything). **Teague cutaway ≈2,400** (days 113–115: at Millrace, the five not back; the walk south to look; the rim's ground read in lantern light, the crossbows, "declaring"; holding the rim at dawn without being asked; no crew names).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:23:- **Pike says the Fallow line before the door is shut;** it costs a line (eleventh; "Teague's ten up"). Then what the wall cannot say: thirty years, forty-odd crews, nobody over a line and back, "Six in and six out, and the sixth a healer." **The room updates** without a word (the hide-woman, the crew of three gone grey, the carter from the first week, the boy). **Teague stands** when they come in and sits at "eleventh."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:25:- **The council, the second honest collision:** Lira for walking away (the fence at forty and the walk at fifty, and pace the third circle on their own time); Brom ("Three hundred's a number a man doesn't reach for." — his father and the horse); Karis ("I would go alone."); **Seln: "Take it… People have faces. Six years I've wanted a face."** Cael's sentence to the whole table (protected), then why: the assumption is wrong and cannot be known to be wrong. **Brom quotes Rooke**, the first person he has ever quoted: "Doors open both ways… I don't like it. I'm in." Lira: "I want it entered that I said walk away." The log (EXC-B7-002). Pike marks HOLD unasked and says it to the room. **Teague at the door** (protected): "If you're late back, we'll come look." / "Noted.", the first *Noted* to anyone above them on the wall.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:29:- **Day 114, the trap (≈9,000–10,500 across two chapters).** The crossing in Seln's order. **The bolt at forty meters**: "Ridge." Six hooded on the rim in road grey (two south, two east, one west, one north). **The Anchor course** closing the line behind them; Cael sees it with perception only. Bolts skip off the fused plate. **Lira runs *down***, and the unit follows. **Forty steps.** The chamber, ten strides square, its ceiling the floor; walls carved; at the middle "something cased… a cord," unread. **The doorway**: "They can shoot the bowl… They can't shoot the stair." **Oryn without hands**: lamp, eyes, two fingers; "Tape it. Leave the bolt."; "the bolt's the plug"; "I came south for exactly this. Enter that." Lira's mend reopened on the stair wall. **The stalemate, given room**: the square of grey going white and grey; a bolt sent down to stop at the thirty-first step; Brom grey and not worse; Karis with her back to the wall she would give a year to read. The design read aloud ("It thinks the floor did the same thing to all six of us."). **The order:** up alone with the one he was given. Oryn: "Ask first." / "I'm not reading anyone." / "I know. I'm saying the rule out loud so it's been said on this floor too." Lira: "Later." **The ascent, Shadow alone**, across the bowl unseen; the rim scanning for a shout that cannot exist. Anchor let off at ten meters as perception, then as a hand: **the knot found and released**, the course going slack like rigging. **Over the stone, declaring**: Wind, Storm seeding the rut, Compression at contact, Ember held out. He removes one man from the plan and does not fight him. The rim breaks as professionals break. The west one looks back for a second, hood up, nothing in it. Four crossbows left; no faces. "Back."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:28:- **Day 96, the perimeter (≈4,000, measured set piece):** procedure said once (Lira the instrument a stride inside; Karis on the line with the cord; Brom marking; Seln ahead; Oryn at the stone; Cael writing counts). The bend in Karis's wrist; **iron at the third cord**; sixty-two cords and twenty strides; ten cords to the middle; "A circle is a made shape." said once as geometry and not followed. **The stake**: registry stamp, thirty-one, a boot's width on the line, "Five years in the weather. A winter either side."; "You drive them where you've measured to."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:21:Deliver Arc 3's promise whole before anything complicates it: a country with roads and no paper, an institution (the board) that prices outcome and never tier, and a discipline (the hold) that turns four years of not-using into the only competence that pays. Teach the system hard. Turns and promises:
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:25:- **Lowmarch, day 9, and the board read like the Cinder House board.** Fourteen slips, not one pricing the crew. Pike: sixties, one arm, "Copper, Force, thirty years on the roads." "Walk, carry, climb, fight." / "In that order?" / "Depends on the day." A heading opened with five names and five columns: Job, Hirer, Witness, Outcome, Price. No tier column. He reads it upside down and looks for the missing column "the way you look for a stair in the dark, with a foot."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:145:| **Seln** | 7,600 (2.5%) | M1: 1,800 (days 10–40: walking every road out of Lowmarch, and later Thornwater, alone; the report nobody asks for) · M5: 2,000 (day 97, at the stone, then the stake: the maps with holes unlocking; ends as he asks for the carter's map) · M7: 2,200 (night of day 112: the second slip held against the first in his head; six years carrying a case; wanting a face) · M8: 1,600 (days 124–128: the ledger in his coat on the road home; giving it to Karis) | His fifteen years; the maps he carried and their blanks; the registry's form-prose; the case's known contents (the machine's maintenance records, read in B6); his read of the trap; his anger | Where the Quieting file is or what it says ("I carried the maps. I never saw the file."); any face or name on the rim; the case opened; the index decoded; the stroke-and-bar decoded; any sentence of affection said aloud |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:260:- The Vastin window (Ch16), substance exact, three sentences: Vastin received the broker's completion report as a courtesy copy, forwarded through a registry office that had no interest in any board east of the Line, in the second folder of the morning, marked *Fallow Ring: crew returned, instruments not recovered*. He read it twice — a broker's report from a town on no registry map, on his desk with no routing note — and did not know why it had reached him, and filed that, in the register of a man who had never once in forty years pretended to knowledge he lacked, as the whole of what he knew about it. He returned the copy to its folder unannotated.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:265:- Vell (Ch9): *Filed with your record. It reads: left in good standing, undefeated on paper. I've kept this ledger forty years and never had a line like it. The session still stands. The road still runs through Ardenmere. — V.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:273:- Ch2, the first pole: *No instrument out here reads me. No Arbiter station, no assessment panel, no registry seat with a seal on it. The board reads what we did. I've spent four years being the case the instruments couldn't parse, and it turns out the cure was a country with no instruments. Write it plainly, because it's true: I'm free. First time.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:274:- Ch3, the seal: *Seln did the shadow work tonight. I didn't. Out here there's a ledger and a ferry west once a month, and a defector's tradecraft in my hands would tell anyone who reads carefully where I learned it. The seal holds. Different country, same arithmetic.* — and *First honest number anyone's written about us in a year. It says four of five got hurt. It's right.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:291:- Ch20: *Instruments recovered. The contract's paid, and the man who posted it is never going to see them, because Seln's keeping the ledger and I'm keeping the kit. Someone measured this place five years ago and wrote bearing and stopped. Karis has a straightedge. She's been waiting her whole life to use it. The Ring, the Stair, and whatever's on that bearing. Pike said a handful. We have two. The kit says three. We're going to go look.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:295:- Ch24, the inventory: *Ten confirmed fragments.* / *Wind-adjacent — Lira. Pressure-adjacent — the Bronze from Ardenmere. Iron-adjacent — Brom. Compression-adjacent — Reydan. Ember-adjacent — Karis. Shadow-adjacent — Seln; source protected; the seal held past the Line as it held inside, and was used twice out here where no one who could carry it west could see it, and that is the seal's whole logic and it is unchanged. Storm-adjacent — Daeva. Anchor-adjacent — unnamed; the hand with no face; opened a door on a rim and held a floor in a hall, and I own a piece of the craft the system uses to hold people and have used it twice this year, once each way. Blade-adjacent — Ephram. Tide-adjacent — Oryn; partial; Iron; self and contact; the tenth, and the first that does nothing in a fight, and the only one whose engagement field says clinical, and the only one with a rule on it in her hand and mine: ask first, every time. Deployment notes current on all ten.* / *One anomaly. Session nine. Tide-adjacent. Not an entry any more; a location. The still place. Read three times. Doesn't flow. Doesn't change. Everything goes around it. Not the Quiet. Not a fragment. Older than the log. Observation continues.* / *Reydan will get his answer. Daeva will get her rematch. Both are going to need a map.* — **Audio rule:** Feryn's name never appears in a list run beside Oryn's; every inventory says "the Bronze from Ardenmere."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:305:- Ch8: Pike: "Quiet ground's where the sigil goes to sleep. Yours. Everyone's. You walk a road, and there's a place on it where your Arbiter stops — not slows; stops — and you walk on past and it's back. There's a handful of them. Along the void roads, all of them. Carters walk round them, and have as long as there've been carters. The dogs live in them. Stillhounds. Nobody's asked them why. Why any of it, nobody knows and nobody's needed to, because the rule's *don't go in*, and the rule's never once failed anybody who kept it." … "That's what a carter knows. That's what I know. There's not a man on the ferry knows a word more." — "I've walked past the Fallow Ring two hundred times. Never once stepped over the line. Thirty years on the roads and I've never met a practitioner who did it twice." — Karis: "What's the line?" / Pike: "You'll know," he said. "Your Arbiter tells you. It stops." — Seln: "Somebody wrote this who learned to write inside."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:307:- Ch10: Karis: "Sixty-two cords and twenty strides," … "Twelve hundred and fifty-six meters, and a piece." … "A circle is a made shape." — Lira: "like a clock that stopped and started again without losing the time." — Seln: "You drive them where you've measured to. Not where you've measured from." … "Five years in the weather. A winter either side." — Brom: "Skin." — Karis: "It costs nothing. There's nothing to spend." — Seln: "I've a knife and fifteen years. It was never most of what I do." — Oryn: "Nothing. Not nothing in him. Nothing in my hands." … "A healer's hands stop working there." — Cael: "It was dark before," … "It's dark now." — Karis: "None I own. And I own more than the registry prints." — Seln: "They live in here because nothing that walks in can fight."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:309:- Ch12: Seln: "They surveyed it," … "Five years ago by the stake, maybe six. They paced the circles and stamped the stakes and drew the maps with holes where the circles are. That's not ignorance. Ignorance doesn't stamp iron." — "The Compact knows what quiet ground does," … "And it's filed somewhere we can't reach." — "No," … "I carried the maps. I never saw the file. I'm not going to draw you one." — Karis (written): *Blank. Stamped. Filed.* — Seln: "We just told them. The report goes west on the next ferry. It'll say we came out." — Oryn: "Six is wrong. I'm a stop." / "They'll write six," Seln said. — Oryn: "I can't mend what I can't read. That's the rule."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:310:- Ch13: Oryn: "You don't get a yes. You get told." — Karis: "Ephram fought you in earnest and the notice said non-hostile. This is earnest and it isn't a fight at all." … "The model doesn't say the engagement has to be a fight. It says it has to be real." — Seln: "That's not consent. It's the nearest thing to it the log's ever had, and it's still not it. I'd enter both." — Lira: "She asked to read you," … "She didn't ask for the rest. Those aren't the same sentence." — Oryn's twenty-minute report: "I can feel that there's movement. More than one. I can't count them — I can't find where one stops. There's no channel. Everyone has a channel; I feel the banks and I know the Path. I can't find the banks in you. I've looked for twenty minutes. It isn't that you're broken. It's that I can't find anything shaped like the thing I read." — "Eleven years. I've never had my hands in something and not known what it was." — "Something just changed," she said. "In you. While I was in there." / "Yes." / "Did I do that?" / "No. I did." … "I need to tell you what I am." / "Then lie still while you do it. You've been still for twenty minutes. I want to see if you can manage twenty-one."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:314:- Ch17: Pike: "Eleventh. Teague's ten up." … "I'd not take it." — Seln: "That's not a wage. That's a lure, cut to fit." … "This isn't a contract. It's a pre-restriction inventory. They've mapped what we do inside, and they've priced a floor where we can't do it." / Karis: "They don't know about Cael." / "They don't need to." … "They want the case. The boy's the price of the case." — "They'll send people. A lure's no use if nobody's waiting at the end of it. People have faces. Six years I've wanted a face." — Cael: "Inside the circle, I'm the only one who works. They chose a floor that makes the rest of you helpless. They don't know it doesn't do anything to me." — Brom: "Doors open both ways," … "I don't like it. I'm in." — Lira: "I want it entered that I said walk away. I was right. We're going anyway." — Teague: "You're taking the Stair contract." / "Yes," Cael said. / "It's a bad contract." / "Yes." … "My crew's at Millrace in two days," Teague said. "If you're late back, we'll come look." / "Noted."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:321:- Ch24: Pike: "Teague says you need a column I don't have. I've kept this ledger thirty years. First time it's been wrong about a crew by being too small." — the carters: "Eleventh," / "Aye," — Teague: "Spring. Whatever's on that bearing. My crew comes." / "Noted," — Pike: "Fence. Forty. Teague says it's yours if you want it; he's got the winter road," / Brom: "Ours," — Lira: "She'll say when," / Brom: "Spring," — *The sites were on an alignment. Not random.* — Karis: "Someone made this pattern." (said once; nobody answers) — **Closing, exact:** "I have ten things that aren't a Path," Cael said, eventually, to nobody in particular, "no tier, no rank, no file I can see — and five people, one of them on a route, who've walked into the quiet three times and come out." He turned it over once and let it stand. "And a line on a map that somebody drew before there was a registry to draw one." / Lira, one-armed, feeding the fire: "Then we follow it." / Brom: "Spring." / Karis, writing: "Noted." / Down the fire, the man who used to file reports about him watched the snow on the ferry landing with evident professional approval and said nothing, which — from him — was home. / Nothing out here had read him. At three floors older than any registry, every Path in the party had stopped at a line and his had not; a fourth had been paced from outside and not crossed. Nobody alive — least of all him — knew why. Someone had made the pattern. That was as far as anyone could say.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:354:- **C5 · Brom's title.** Ch3: Brom answering teeth "for three years and a Copper Crown." The Copper Crown was Lira's (B4). Brom's is the continental Copper title (B5/B6; B6 Ch23's "continental Copper title"). **Render as his continental title.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:356:- **C7 · Oryn's age.** "Late twenties" (Ch6, Cael's catalogue) against "Eleven years. I've never had my hands in something…" (Ch13). With Kindling LOCKED at fourteen, that makes her about twenty-five. **Recommend** never stating her age. "Late twenties" stays Cael's estimate; "eleven years" stands.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:362:- **Already ruled elsewhere and followed here:** Bracken is *he* (OWNER-DECISIONS #7). Vastin's "forty years" is his own rounding, with no age stated (Book 8 ruling 20; OWNER-DECISIONS #8). The narration uses "the academy above Ostrand" (Book 8 decision 9). Registry collisions are not renamed in this edition.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:8:- Owner names: canon only. The miller, Millrace's ford-keeper and patients, the six on the rim, the second Anchor specialist, the hide-woman, the crew of three and Teague's crew stay unnamed. **No faces on the rim.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:26:- **Millrace (day 113):** the wheel heard before the roofs; the ford-keeper's "Five off the ridge" / "I know." **Oryn's table**: fifteen, three serious (a crushed hand, a child's chest, an old woman's knee with a ladder in it) and a dozen small with one hand each. **Ask first, refused** ("You asked. That's the rule and you kept it. The answer's no. Next."), entered first. Karis: "She was curious about you. Enter that somewhere." **Her arithmetic aloud**, finger by finger. "You're asking me to break the route." / "I'm not asking. I'm telling you where we'll be." / "That's worse. That's a healer's sentence." "I'm not going to be anybody's sixth." **Word sent up the route** by carter (late, how late, why, where to send for the child). **Terms** (protected). Lira's sixth-chair line. The fork log.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:9:- POV: Cael ≈27,300. **Oryn cutaway ≈2,000** (day 100, the stool after the telling, the covenant page on her knee; what a healer does with having been a source; no theory). **Karis cutaway ≈2,600** (the week of tables: the tally of kinds she will not say; *the Quieting* chosen because it is the right grammar; **the pen held over the page, and the hypothesis never stated**). **Lira cutaway ≈2,000** (the bowman's lessons: shooting braced, one-armed, with a bow someone else spans). **Vastin ≈300** (the courtesy copy; three sentences, substance exact). **Oryn cutaway ≈1,800** (dawn on the 111th onward: north out of the gate with a spare rope, having left her mule with the crew; the route, the debt she set, the line she tested; ends before Millrace's table).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:10:- Formula load: progression vocabulary ≈40 per 10k. ≈18 growth beats. Supporting beats for all six, plus Pike (by copy), Vastin and the bowman.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:25:- **The birthday (day 102):** Lira instigates one-armed, pays one-handed, and has been practising the pouch for a week without saying so. Brom acquires three kinds ("Three."). Six places in the common room. Oryn at the table "like a woman who has sat at a great many tables and stayed at none of them." **The line written** (protected). "A stop. Good. Write it down before it changes." **Pike's Fallow copy** by carter; "Six went in. Six came out." beside Gault's last note. Hesk's package does not come, and the absence sits at the table unremarked. Seln: "He's counted her… So has the broker." The apples argument, which Karis loses on the merits.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:30:- **Day 110.** Lira first at the gate-walk at dusk, in the order he has had for fifteen days (protected exchange); the fighter's question ("It felt like a Third-day."); her hand along the plank to his boot; "Then six." **The circle of six**: what each of the four saw, in order; Karis's five findings said; Seln's "Yet."; Oryn's "I'm not going to guess past it."; nobody puts a verb between the facts; the four wheres; "We find the others…"; "One at a time, for money." Oryn: "North in the morning… Don't go in without me…"; her hand on Seln's shoulder. **Brom at the ladder** ("It's a count. You like counts."). **The Vastin window** (three sentences). **Oryn at the well**: the rule written while she watches (protected); "Once is a morning" (the debt's terms set by her: three readings on different days, then all of it at once); "Don't read anyone on the road to find out whether you can."; the note written under the rule. **The second pole** in the log (protected).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:39:- Vastin: one window only, three sentences, no age. "Forty years" is his rounding.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:8:- Owner names: canon only. Teague's crew (including the older healer of no Path), the hide carter, the ferryman and his boy, the old woman at Thornwater, the carters at the fire and the inn's keeper stay unnamed. **The fourth site stays unnamed.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:10:- Formula load: progression vocabulary ≈50 per 10k (the line's mechanics as trials: Arbiter, sigil, declaration, render). ≈18 growth beats. Supporting beats for all five, plus Oryn, Pike, Teague, Ephram, Vell.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:25:- **Day 91:** marked at the plank in front of eleven witnesses. The mail: **Ephram** and **Vell** (texts protected). **The void road (day 92):** the registry's printed sheet against the ground (seven dashed roads ending in white; this is the third); Karis's carter's map with three blank circles; "Their map has no roads. His has no quiet ground. Between them you get the country." Ephram's letter read at the wash at noon (Bracken told the registry "the Line and nothing past it"; Lira: "Good."). Vell's read at noon on the 94th, aloud, to Lira ("She puts the thing that decides it last." / "So does Ephram.").
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:39:- Ephram's letter carries "Bracken" (he). Vell's carries "The session still stands," unexplained.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-003.md:8:- Owner names: canon only. Oxhollow's ford-keeper, the smith, the patients at Oxhollow's table and Teague's crew stay unnamed. Of Oryn's seven holds, only Oxhollow and Thornwater are named.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:30:- **Lowmarch, day 49 — the board anatomized:** a woman captain's line read before and after; the eleven-bale captain ("Say it again and I'll write it"); "The book's for me. The saying's for them."; the wall at the lower inn; "A Bronze who lost my carter…"; "Did you ever hear of a ledger-keeper called Vell?" / "No."; Seln's finger on the carter's map, the asset-restriction **said once and put away**, the map turned east. "Four lines. Nobody lost, nobody hurt, nobody knows you." Brom: "Eleven."
