  1082	- **Lira:** "Six"; "as if it were a ladder"; crosses a floor arguing; "Don't come"; "Next time, say. Even if I bite."; "On the right"; "That's after the ruling."; "Don't be kind."; "I know you liked it."; "It's mine."; "*Door. It's held.*"
  1083	- **Karis:** "Then what am I writing?"; "I'll write it as if it were ground. That's my cost."; "Say it as if it mattered."; the floor and the cord; "Files change"; "I can't promise you the room" taken with a nod; the bread passed.
  1084	- **Brom:** the docket he can't read; "Can it be taught?"; the gate's top hinge; "Me."; "I check."; "The left's back" earned; the envelope; "It's the kindest thing anybody's done for me on this hill."; the strap.
  1085	- **Seln:** "Mm"; "You should not."; "Do not take me for a pattern."; written down as what he is doing; five beans; "It is the first time in a good many years that anybody has come back up a road in the dark to look for me."
  1086	- **Ephram:** stays for the frames; the plates in order of weight; a ruled line; "I'm not asking… He didn't, did he."
  1087	- **Withrow:** "I would rather you had the right figure under mine than a guess."
  1088	- **Bracken:** *Nothing sealed*; "fourteen"; the same Fifth-day, "because nobody else was going to"; "I ask when, not why."
  1089	- **Rooke:** "Now."; "Your head hasn't heard."; two words on a card; "It is."
  1090	- **Gault:** "I have written that down."
  1091	- **The house's counsel:** "You look as if you'd expected it since breakfast"; "Sit up straight tomorrow. It's nearly the last time you'll have to."
  1092	- **Jent:** "Your table was better than ours."; "I would rather hear her than read her."
  1093	- **Hesk:** "Eat something green."
