  1123	
  1124	- **The recess (flag):** two weeks; about forty enrollees stay by slip (*Remaining in residence. Reason:*); the program runs through it; no wing three; the records hall "keeps no recess".
  1125	- **Hesk's recess letter (text mine, ch41).**
  1126	- **The lodge's road column in recess** and its foot line *Two at the road foot, changed at the bell. Two at the landing.* A tin cup.
  1127	- **The farm (flag):** the bluff's south slope — kitchen gardens, upper and lower orchard, a stream along the bottom hedge to the water meadows, the farm track from the stable passage through the orchard gate to the meadow gate (about four hundred yards), the gardener's cottage (a gate dropped on its top hinge; a dog). **The gardener:** unnamed, thirty years with the house's trees.
  1128	- **Seln's road-craft (flag):** camp forty paces from water, "of the shortest person present" (water covers a voice at forty paces and a foot at ten; things walk to water at night; wet ground); the open approach (down the middle of the track, in daylight, hands seen, stop and be looked at); two watches of four hours, two to a watch, the fifth sleeps through and rotates; oilcloth twice, pencil not ink, nothing written at the bottom of a load, "whatever you would grieve to lose rides on a person"; forty pounds for a day, thirty for thirty days. The night-road drill: hand on the shoulder in front; halts; a head-count by touch.
  1129	- **Brom counts (flag):** "I check." — he counts again when the first count is right.
