editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:13:| Cael | Sixteen (turned on the eleventh of Sowing, Book 4; the date is never set beside a season word, OWNER #35). Healthy, rested, and trained: sixty-one floor sessions over the recess. No current injuries: B4 closed him fit (the quarter-burst's hip load ended the night of the twenty-third of Reaping; the plate's right-shoulder ache eased by the week's end). The leading hip carries the Wind fragment's old strain (crest to inner knee after a hard evening), and the landing beat is still unshortened. The right shoulder pays Pressure, "four blows a sitting", the circle's private cap and not a registry schedule (B4 ch62; OWNER #36: the plate/Pressure shoulder is the right). The Shadow fragment's rent runs from waking, spent or not; drifts come in the gaps, never in the work, and the weekly count is falling; the working ledger's day count since the stair and the protocol *Hold. First.* are the discipline. Arbiter dark since the Kindling. [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05] |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:14:| Lira | Wind Path, Iron-tier, Rank One, formal: the Ostrand registry station's Arbiter evaluation on the fifth of the new month, fifty-one minutes ("They didn't give me anything today. They caught up."); the porter changed the word and moved her name the next day; Gault filed, Ilsev witnessing. Season record certified "Eleven bouts unbeaten. None lost." The Copper Crown is retired on the shelf over the settle ("There. It's retired."). Fit: the semifinal's hip strain (deep, nothing torn) had a month's knitting left at term's end, and nothing of it carries into this book. She trains at dawn on Rooke's speed line. She meant to write to Fiske over the recess (Fiske: "North tier, next season. I'll be watching the Iron bracket."); whether she did is open to M1–M3. [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05] |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:16:| Karis | Karis (Dellenmoor), Ember Path, Iron Rank Three (unchanged all B4). Fit. She spent ten weeks of the recess on the clause argument, in the named top-floor reading room (*Reading room. Assigned: K. Dellenmoor.*, Bracken's hand, standing through the recess). [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05] |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:17:| Seln | Shadow Path, Bronze. Teaching assistant in the assessment wing (the copying table behind the counter; his one sound, "Mm"); the recess counter sheet names *S. Seln* against every working day of the recess and nobody else. At his desk the whole recess. The quarterly went out sealed on the twenty-sixth of Reaping: *Continuation of embedded coverage recommended.* [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05] |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:20:| Vastin | The Archmarshal Vastin (his B4 title throughout, ch38–59). Last seen in B4 at the posting-house at the turn of the registry road on the evening of the twenty-fourth of Reaping, writing the file note and a four-sentence private letter to Bracken. His desk in the Compact's western administration (third floor, river side) is the source's, not B4's, and stands only until the text says otherwise. **No stated age** (§12 C2; OWNER #8, #17); career "forty years". His left hand "had begun to dislike evenings as well as mornings". [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05] |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:24:**Cael knows:** his six fragments, with their costs and deployment rules (the ch62 inventory: "Six and an anomaly. It isn't a seventh anything."); that the mechanism is integration of witnessed abilities under the stakes conditions; the line the four signed at Halcenvane the year before, the minute of three numbered rules (conditions not manufactured; a directed acquisition only within earnest engagement the other party begins, awake and directed; full cost written beforehand), for which *directed, open-eyed, or not at all* is this book's shorthand and never B4's wording; that Seln has functionally switched (the corridor on the twenty-seventh; the unchanged rotations; the recess counter sheet) and that "Gratitude is the leak"; that one unsigned slip of wing paper came to him inside a returned coursework folder on the night of the Copper final, learned and burned on the common-room coals, and that he and Karis alone know it; that Vastin wrote a note he believes says he is not an error (inferred, not seen; OWNER #10; "in a hand I'd wager signs its whole name"); that the Level 4 designation exists and nobody can trace it; that the fielding clause exists, with its text verbatim (sixth part, subsection four); the year's finding, "The system isn't confused about me"; and the tournament's three-year cycle and Norhold as this cycle's host. He does **not** know the Standard's mechanics yet (that comes in the map room); the exhibition provision's wording; the squad clause; Daeva beyond rumor; what Seln's reports said; or anything about the office above Vastin. [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:26:**Only the circle (Lira, Brom, Karis) knows the mechanism.** Seln does not, and nor do Ephram, Rooke, Withrow, Bracken, Gault, Hesk or Vastin. Rooke suspects a gap between Cael's record and his ceiling and has chosen never to ask.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:28:**Karis knows:** the fielding clause (sixth part, subsection four; copied and banked on the twelfth of the new month: "Interesting." / "It's banked."); its forty-year history (the placement scandal) and that the charter predates the last registry standardization (both the source's, to be taught in M1); the retired word's passage: read, in her Greyvane notebooks, identified to the directive's terminology article, voiced once at Halcenvane (B4 ch50, the word lower-case in her mouth, one factual clause) and closed as *Why retire a working method?*; the notebooks went by hand-cart (four loads) to the named top-floor room on the night of the twenty-seventh, Bracken's card in ninety seconds, and the archive sweep of the tenth found carrel eleven *nil*. She will find the bracket rule (*no tier seeding applicable … demonstration-exhibition provisions*) on the second day of drafting. She saw a slip burned on the common-room coals and asked nothing. She keeps the marbled watcher log. [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:30:**Seln knows:** everything the office sees; the two components he saw at the pin (forward Wind into a live hazard; contact absorption) and filed without, category two unused; that Jask has "quick off a read"; that the compilation came home unmarked and is "one of three. probably the third."; the slip he wrote once and squared; the records-broker's tasking pattern (still unreconciled; B5's own); and that the bank and the circle exist only by inference from outcomes. He does **not** know the mechanism or the Shadow acquisition, and no sentence states his reason for switching (the B4 rule continues). [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:32:**Vastin knows:** his own evaluation and file note (*Classification error is unlikely. Continue observation.*, signed with his whole name; the handsome sentence struck at the close and the amendment written that night); that the designation on the enrollee's sheet was entered by the Kindling in the file's first minutes and that nobody at any height has since amended or questioned it ("So the record was not broken. It was doing something.", which he did not write); the wing's six filings, read once and put "a good way under the record"; nothing of fragments; nothing of Seln's null reports. Whether he knows the Level 4 watch by name is not on B4's page (BOOK_MAP §5 allows it in his cutaways). [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:38:- **Cael:** the Power Log (the old volume, near its last leaves; Hesk's bound volume arrives at the rest day), the year's inventory closed on the last night of term with Hesk's steel drafting pen; the observation notebook, with Hesk's reply and the birthday note behind its front board; Vell's letter (five short sentences, her mark and the circuit ledger's stamp); Hesk's travel clock (inaccurate; he sets it an hour fast during tournament weeks); a copy of Bracken's sanding habit; currency in marks (he does not spend much). [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:39:- **Enrollment:** the demonstration provision of the assay clause, with one semester stamp, renewed (Bracken's line in the enrollment book on the twenty-second of Reaping; Gault's note of the twentieth: growth confirmed in five, the plate flat; the record keeps five capabilities, two of them public). Gault is the evaluator of record. Next term's sitting is already ruled on his calendar, the provision's half-yearly evaluation: *Panel of record: Gault, with two. Measured against: baseline (entry), and the note of the twentieth of Reaping.*; same instruments, checked on Fourth-days; the frame to get a new second notch. So the mill-town session (M2) is the provision's SECOND evaluation, not its third (§12 C8). The panel "travels" (a seals case with a handle) is the source's, to be staged in M1. [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:40:- **Delegation:** two wagons; travel roster of eleven (five competitors, Rooke, Gault, two third-year reserves, a wagoner, and S. Seln for *records and floor scheduling*). The roster line carries the registry name *Caelen Hesk-ward, 41-7843-V* once, so the schedule office's "C. Cael" reads as its abbreviation (§10 item 6). Fourteen of the hill's students are Silver and one is Gold (B4 ch8), and none is fielded; M1 says why in one sentence. Withrow and Bracken travel for the fourth meet and Norhold. Bracken's pouch is the delegation's letter route from Movement 3 on (Karis's information policy). [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:41:- **Documents:** three copies and a certified transcription of the tournament charter (Karis read it on the afternoon of Withrow's address; Withrow: posted before selection); Bracken's certified season sheets (about three hundred, across the recess); Karis's grey notebook (the clause and *Interesting.*; Ember's three words) and her marbled watcher log; Rooke's profiles table (forty-one names); Seln's cipher page in the small case (the quarterly is gone down the fish steps); Vastin's file note in the Compact's folder (nobody on the bluff has seen it) and his four-sentence private letter to Bracken praising the enrollment index (sent by the morning post; whether Bracken has shown it to anyone is open); and, from Movement 2, the Standard's public documentation (forty pages) and the examiner's annotated manual. [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:47:| 1 | Wind-adjacent | Lira | Working ceiling **six bursts free on the sprung oak** (stone fewer; the seventh billed to the next morning, the eighth to the morning after), measured by the panel on the twentieth; unchanged all recess ("the cost structure is the thing to work on"). Landing beat locked and unshortened (ch62: "Three years of trying to trim it"; B5's inventories count four, N9). The quarter-burst, shut mid-payment once: "one point isn't a line", not in the column. Public at documented rate [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05] |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:52:| 6 | Shadow-adjacent | Seln (Bronze; non-combat; directed, unknowing: "in the third hour of a bad night, on a stair") | Presence-suppression and movement-masking, mutually exclusive in his hands. Rent from waking, spent or not; drifts in the gaps, never in the work, fewer every week. **Deployment: none, anywhere, ever**; "Useful where: nowhere yet. Second year of that answer begins now." Seln is not told [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05] |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:55:- **Public record ("the bank"):** the suite at documented rates only. Compression is on no wing record (its only paper is the Ardenmere circuit record); Pressure is flat on every Halcenvane plate and public only in that same circuit record; Shadow is unknown to every record. This is the doctrine (Vell's "fight to the record"). [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:62:| Lira | Oldest partner (four years by B5's count, N8); reads the log; gives him arguments out loud when he goes quiet. She has stopped carrying "the case" into bouts and is now "just carrying her kit." She named him in writing to hear her advancement filing (B4 ch52), and he has her account of the station's four seconds. Iron Rank One is hers by the Arbiter's reading ("They caught up."), and the crown is on the shelf. [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05] |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:64:| Karis | Banked the clause for him; shows him her notebook (a habit since the inspection term, the audit's C6 wording in place of the source's season word; never remarked on). Was wrong about Seln and asked for it to be written down. Saw the slip burned and asked nothing. [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05] |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:65:| Seln | The counter, "Thank you for the form," "Mm," every week by design. One slip, once (the night of the Copper final), burned on the common-room coals; no "stove protocol" exists yet, and if a second slip ever comes (M8) the stove is the same unspoken procedure. The asymmetry debt "filed under debts, no current mechanism of payment." He sits at the margin of every table; on the wall at dusk he walked off before Cael spoke ("Nobody watched him go."). [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05] |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:68:| Withrow | Chancellor; her ambition is visible and checkable; she declines to make events of procedures. Her address of the twelfth: "Halcenvane Academy will contest the qualifying season.", and the sentence ends there; "this house has not qualified in eighteen years" (B4's own rounding; the convocation keeps "eighteen"). [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05] |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:69:| Bracken | Registrar, twelve years in the office (B4 ch5; never "decades"; "he", OWNER #7); certifies true records; "very careful to make no decision … that was not mine to make." Entered the renewal in the enrollment book; certified every season column at the green table; wrote the named room's card; holds the Archmarshal's four-sentence private letter on his index (unknown to Cael). [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05] |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:72:| Vastin | One interview (B4 ch56: eleven questions in a twelve-by-fourteen room, the twelfth not asked); civil baseline; nothing warmer or colder yet. On the evaluation morning he looked once at the failing frame and not again at Cael that whole morning. He has decided that if the question ever becomes properly his he will ask it "in a room with the door shut and tell the boy first." [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05] |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:83:- Seln's locked case: carried and unopened all book.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:85:- Fiske's door ("North tier, next season. I'll be watching the Iron bracket.") and Lira's intended letter (N6; the author may pay it in M2–M3). [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:91:The first day of the qualifying year is day 0 (convocation), after a recess of twelve weeks and four days. No season is named anywhere in this book; weather words only; no month order, month length or cross-month day count is ever stated (OWNER #35, #36.4, #37 O1). Halcenvane's weekdays are the office's First-day … Seventh-day; English names appear only inside Daeva's window at Norhold (#37 O4). The first meet falls about five weeks in, the second about three weeks after it, the third "eleven weeks" after Seln's counter sentence, and the fourth at the year's turn in the deep cold; the road to Norhold runs seventeen days with the melt under the wheels; the tournament runs about three weeks with a rest day at its midpoint (the birthday: seventeen, the eleventh of Sowing by default, never beside a season word; OWNER #35 may move it to "the third of Reaping"). The road home is seventeen days. See `BOOK_MAP.md` §6. [B4-reconciled 2026-10-05]
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:122:- YEAR COUNTS NOT INCREMENTED (Book 5 ch1 is ~twelve weeks after Book 4 ch62): the landing beat 'three years'; Compression unseen 'two years'; the anomaly 'two years running'; Lira's bursts 'three years'; the watchers 'two years'. Protected item 21's 'three years' unchanged (#37 O3).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:123:- CALENDAR: the response went down on the morning courier of the Sixth-day (d12); the memorandum's fourteen-day deadline lapsed on d21, crossed off, Bracken did not resubmit ('a true record… did not get any truer for being sent twice'); the card came up on the Fifth-day (d25): 'Thirteen days'. No season names ('A note for the cold term.'); house weekdays; no month order.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:124:- Bracken known 'a year'; the clause 'forty years ago, before you were born'; Seln on 'the last line' of the roster list. The charter's founding articles are older than the schedule where Karis found the provision and older than the clause, 'before the registry's last standardization'.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:125:- New canon accepted: the fourteen Silver students and one Gold on the hill are teaching fellows (the fellows' book, not the enrollment record); Vastin's recess room unlocated; the routing slip carries TWO INITIALS Vastin cannot place (new private thread — unresolved; carry forward); Hesk's reply letter; the buried Copper Rank Four is 'she'; seeds for M2: the page Karis marked in Rooke's manual; the wool town's pine floors.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:130:**Calendar.** Day 0 is convocation, a First-day; Halcenvane weekdays run First-day … Seventh-day, and Fifth-days fall on days 4, 11, 18 and 25. No season is named. No month is named, and no month order is given. The only date-names in the movement are the B4 recollections (the eleventh of Sowing; the note of the twentieth of Reaping). The first meet falls on about day 35, two days' drive south (the wool town).
