editions/monroe-1.3/book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:166:- **Cael** knows the Standard's architecture (marks, strikes, par thirty, the bands, weighting, exhibitions rated for the figure only). He has priced Lira, Brom and Ephram correctly ahead of the panel. He knows the abbreviation on the card and that some unseen hand let the advisory go through; he does not know Vastin wrote it. He saw Karis mark a page in Rooke's manual (he does not know which), and he saw her write a note in the founding articles (he does not know what).
