editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:33:- "Compact" is said aloud **once** (Seln). Nothing about where the file is, what it says, or why. No dating past "five years… maybe six."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:21:Deliver Arc 3's promise whole before anything complicates it: a country with roads and no paper, an institution (the board) that prices outcome and never tier, and a discipline (the hold) that turns four years of not-using into the only competence that pays. Teach the system hard. Turns and promises:
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:25:- **Lowmarch, day 9, and the board read like the Cinder House board.** Fourteen slips, not one pricing the crew. Pike: sixties, one arm, "Copper, Force, thirty years on the roads." "Walk, carry, climb, fight." / "In that order?" / "Depends on the day." A heading opened with five names and five columns: Job, Hirer, Witness, Outcome, Price. No tier column. He reads it upside down and looks for the missing column "the way you look for a stair in the dark, with a foot."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:23:- **The cascade: it listens, it doesn't pull (three nights).** His own current at the edge of every thought; the nine coming up out of it one at a time and told apart by sound; "a room he had lived in for eighteen years with the lights suddenly on." Brom on the ladder ("How many people." / "Nine. Ten. I can't hear the tenth. It's the thing I'm hearing with." / the forge story). Day two: **Storm heard resettling** in the yard, a hand on the well's rim; the ground arriving half a beat late under a counted foot, so he **relearns the Wind economy in the yard** while the listening runs (a learning encounter). **Oryn's "Where is it loudest."** "Here… It's not louder there. It's nearer." Ask first, said in the yard: "I ask the dying." / "I ask first. Every time."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:9:- POV: Cael ≈35,400. **Seln cutaway ≈2,200** (night of day 112, after the council: the two slips laid side by side in his head; six years carrying a case for people he cannot see; why he wants a face; he may not open the case or decode anything). **Teague cutaway ≈2,400** (days 113–115: at Millrace, the five not back; the walk south to look; the rim's ground read in lantern light, the crossbows, "declaring"; holding the rim at dawn without being asked; no crew names).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:23:- **Pike says the Fallow line before the door is shut;** it costs a line (eleventh; "Teague's ten up"). Then what the wall cannot say: thirty years, forty-odd crews, nobody over a line and back, "Six in and six out, and the sixth a healer." **The room updates** without a word (the hide-woman, the crew of three gone grey, the carter from the first week, the boy). **Teague stands** when they come in and sits at "eleventh."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:145:| **Seln** | 7,600 (2.5%) | M1: 1,800 (days 10–40: walking every road out of Lowmarch, and later Thornwater, alone; the report nobody asks for) · M5: 2,000 (day 97, at the stone, then the stake: the maps with holes unlocking; ends as he asks for the carter's map) · M7: 2,200 (night of day 112: the second slip held against the first in his head; six years carrying a case; wanting a face) · M8: 1,600 (days 124–128: the ledger in his coat on the road home; giving it to Karis) | His fifteen years; the maps he carried and their blanks; the registry's form-prose; the case's known contents (the machine's maintenance records, read in B6); his read of the trap; his anger | Where the Quieting file is or what it says ("I carried the maps. I never saw the file."); any face or name on the rim; the case opened; the index decoded; the stroke-and-bar decoded; any sentence of affection said aloud |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:260:- The Vastin window (Ch16), substance exact, three sentences: Vastin received the broker's completion report as a courtesy copy, forwarded through a registry office that had no interest in any board east of the Line, in the second folder of the morning, marked *Fallow Ring: crew returned, instruments not recovered*. He read it twice — a broker's report from a town on no registry map, on his desk with no routing note — and did not know why it had reached him, and filed that, in the register of a man who had never once in forty years pretended to knowledge he lacked, as the whole of what he knew about it. He returned the copy to its folder unannotated.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:265:- Vell (Ch9): *Filed with your record. It reads: left in good standing, undefeated on paper. I've kept this ledger forty years and never had a line like it. The session still stands. The road still runs through Ardenmere. — V.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:273:- Ch2, the first pole: *No instrument out here reads me. No Arbiter station, no assessment panel, no registry seat with a seal on it. The board reads what we did. I've spent four years being the case the instruments couldn't parse, and it turns out the cure was a country with no instruments. Write it plainly, because it's true: I'm free. First time.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:291:- Ch20: *Instruments recovered. The contract's paid, and the man who posted it is never going to see them, because Seln's keeping the ledger and I'm keeping the kit. Someone measured this place five years ago and wrote bearing and stopped. Karis has a straightedge. She's been waiting her whole life to use it. The Ring, the Stair, and whatever's on that bearing. Pike said a handful. We have two. The kit says three. We're going to go look.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:307:- Ch10: Karis: "Sixty-two cords and twenty strides," … "Twelve hundred and fifty-six meters, and a piece." … "A circle is a made shape." — Lira: "like a clock that stopped and started again without losing the time." — Seln: "You drive them where you've measured to. Not where you've measured from." … "Five years in the weather. A winter either side." — Brom: "Skin." — Karis: "It costs nothing. There's nothing to spend." — Seln: "I've a knife and fifteen years. It was never most of what I do." — Oryn: "Nothing. Not nothing in him. Nothing in my hands." … "A healer's hands stop working there." — Cael: "It was dark before," … "It's dark now." — Karis: "None I own. And I own more than the registry prints." — Seln: "They live in here because nothing that walks in can fight."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:321:- Ch24: Pike: "Teague says you need a column I don't have. I've kept this ledger thirty years. First time it's been wrong about a crew by being too small." — the carters: "Eleventh," / "Aye," — Teague: "Spring. Whatever's on that bearing. My crew comes." / "Noted," — Pike: "Fence. Forty. Teague says it's yours if you want it; he's got the winter road," / Brom: "Ours," — Lira: "She'll say when," / Brom: "Spring," — *The sites were on an alignment. Not random.* — Karis: "Someone made this pattern." (said once; nobody answers) — **Closing, exact:** "I have ten things that aren't a Path," Cael said, eventually, to nobody in particular, "no tier, no rank, no file I can see — and five people, one of them on a route, who've walked into the quiet three times and come out." He turned it over once and let it stand. "And a line on a map that somebody drew before there was a registry to draw one." / Lira, one-armed, feeding the fire: "Then we follow it." / Brom: "Spring." / Karis, writing: "Noted." / Down the fire, the man who used to file reports about him watched the snow on the ferry landing with evident professional approval and said nothing, which — from him — was home. / Nothing out here had read him. At three floors older than any registry, every Path in the party had stopped at a line and his had not; a fourth had been paced from outside and not crossed. Nobody alive — least of all him — knew why. Someone had made the pattern. That was as far as anyone could say.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:337:| The Compact's six-year suppression / directive (B8) | Fieldwork only: stakes (31; 32 twice, one re-surveyed with the stroke-and-bar; 33; the 34 cordon), the maps' blanks, the kit and its ledger, a completion report going west | Policy, files, offices, the word "suppress," any date on the cordon, the stroke-and-bar or the index decoded |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:354:- **C5 · Brom's title.** Ch3: Brom answering teeth "for three years and a Copper Crown." The Copper Crown was Lira's (B4). Brom's is the continental Copper title (B5/B6; B6 Ch23's "continental Copper title"). **Render as his continental title.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:356:- **C7 · Oryn's age.** "Late twenties" (Ch6, Cael's catalogue) against "Eleven years. I've never had my hands in something…" (Ch13). With Kindling LOCKED at fourteen, that makes her about twenty-five. **Recommend** never stating her age. "Late twenties" stays Cael's estimate; "eleven years" stands.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:362:- **Already ruled elsewhere and followed here:** Bracken is *he* (OWNER-DECISIONS #7). Vastin's "forty years" is his own rounding, with no age stated (Book 8 ruling 20; OWNER-DECISIONS #8). The narration uses "the academy above Ostrand" (Book 8 decision 9). Registry collisions are not renamed in this edition.

