book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:28:- **Day 96, the perimeter (≈4,000, measured set piece):** procedure said once (Lira the instrument a stride inside; Karis on the line with the cord; Brom marking; Seln ahead; Oryn at the stone; Cael writing counts). The bend in Karis's wrist; **iron at the third cord**; sixty-two cords and twenty strides; ten cords to the middle; "A circle is a made shape." said once as geometry and not followed. **The stake**: registry stamp, thirty-one, a boot's width on the line, "Five years in the weather. A winter either side."; "You drive them where you've measured to."
book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-004.md:47:Day 96, the sun on the ridge and going: six people a hundred and forty meters inside a perfect circle, at the far lip of a den. The middle box is on Brom's back and the healer's hands don't work. The stone is two hundred meters west. One of them has told nobody that nothing happened to him.
book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:45:The sensation-language of listening, kept to sensation; Thornwater in the back of autumn (ice on the trough, the grain going up the ladder past where they sleep); the tables' daily rhythm; the bowman's manner and words; the birthday's warmth and humor; the shape of each finding scene; all the windows.
book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:29:- **Day 114, the trap (≈9,000–10,500 across two chapters).** The crossing in Seln's order. **The bolt at forty meters**: "Ridge." Six hooded on the rim in road grey (two south, two east, one west, one north). **The Anchor course** closing the line behind them; Cael sees it with perception only. Bolts skip off the fused plate. **Lira runs *down***, and the unit follows. **Forty steps.** The chamber, ten strides square, its ceiling the floor; walls carved; at the middle "something cased… a cord," unread. **The doorway**: "They can shoot the bowl… They can't shoot the stair." **Oryn without hands**: lamp, eyes, two fingers; "Tape it. Leave the bolt."; "the bolt's the plug"; "I came south for exactly this. Enter that." Lira's mend reopened on the stair wall. **The stalemate, given room**: the square of grey going white and grey; a bolt sent down to stop at the thirty-first step; Brom grey and not worse; Karis with her back to the wall she would give a year to read. The design read aloud ("It thinks the floor did the same thing to all six of us."). **The order:** up alone with the one he was given. Oryn: "Ask first." / "I'm not reading anyone." / "I know. I'm saying the rule out loud so it's been said on this floor too." Lira: "Later." **The ascent, Shadow alone**, across the bowl unseen; the rim scanning for a shout that cannot exist. Anchor let off at ten meters as perception, then as a hand: **the knot found and released**, the course going slack like rigging. **Over the stone, declaring**: Wind, Storm seeding the rut, Compression at contact, Ember held out. He removes one man from the plan and does not fight him. The rim breaks as professionals break. The west one looks back for a second, hood up, nothing in it. Four crossbows left; no faces. "Back."
book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:28:- **The Thornwater road (days 41–43), ≈4,000:** the carter at the fire ("Two carts went quiet on it last month"); the stretch at dusk after a wheel cost an hour; positions; the valley's noise; **Lira's hand up at a hole in the noise**; Seln without turning, "Don't declare anything." / "Walk. Same pace."; "I could clear it." / "No." / "I know. I'm saying it so I've said it."; Brom becoming exactly as large as his body and no larger; Karis deciding five times not to take out the notebook; the five items (keeps station at forty meters; makes no sound; tracks the buckle; won't cross the gravel fan; reacts to nothing because they gave it nothing); it stops a hundred meters short of the fence. No blow struck.
book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:49:Day 49: thirteenth of thirteen, with eleven lines between them and Teague. "I'm free. First time." Something out here hunts Paths, and nobody has given them the reason. Teague has read them and been read. The ford clearance, forty marks, sits on the plank with HOLD and his name beside it, and his crew is going out on the autumn road for a week.
book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:16:The second morning after the wall (day 51). Teague's crew went out at the previous dawn on the autumn road and is a week away. The five are thirteenth of thirteen with about ten marks, sleeping in the meadow. Nobody is hurt. Karis holds one word, *stillhound*, underlined.
book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-002.md:37:- Teague is absent: on the autumn road, then back and out again on hold slips. No meeting.
book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:22:- **The Ring (≈8,000–9,500 across two chapters), a retreat with a geometry.** The line is the objective. Nine counted on the white. "The road's cut." / "The grass. Where the cord went." Brom holds the lip: a hand's-height drop that robs a hound of drive, the haft, a man the pack cannot hear. Lira runs the rim's turned edge; the ankle goes a third time; the forearm taken and held; she cannot burst it off. **Brom's bolt through the eye at four meters.** Oryn's hands: "Nothing… Nothing in my hands." Cloth and knees. "Move. I can't fix this here. Move." Brom's string opens his fingers in the dark. The lane counted down, 160 to 60, the scrub moving at Lira's pace and never showing a shape. They are *careless* in here, because no prey has ever shouted. **Karis down at sixty**, hands on a throat, the jaws closing across her fists, the loudest sound on the ring. **Shadow, once, ten strides** (circle and Oryn only). The throw. Then *he stops holding*: Wind full, north off the lane; every head turns; then everything, one after another, so there is never a breath when he is not the loudest thing on the floor. Pressure for noise; Ember held out; Blade ringing with nothing to cut; Storm seeding the rut; Anchor off its hold and looking west. North to the rut, **east the wrong way** about a hundred and twenty meters, back west. Seln's "Back" from the stone and Lira's a breath after. The second lock with Compression at contact. Over the stone. **The bolt at two meters.** Anchor's perception sees Karis's points before they light: **the wall of ignition along the line's inside edge**, from her knees, voiceless. Seven break out north and south along the outside; two dead. Win-sentence and costs on the page. The opponent learned nothing it could use, because it had never needed to.
book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:22:- **The bearing walk (116–118), on the page:** a road, then a track, then a carter's memory. Karis does not once say *if*. The country going into high autumn.
book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:23:- **The Drowned Hall from the rise:** roofless, twelve strides square, a spring through the broken floor, a marsh exactly as wide as the Quiet. "Third." **The line** at the marsh's edge ("Gone"/"Back"); **stake thirty-three** (old, and no second); mud **heaved from below** along the water's edge ("It's never been out."); a bar at the hall's lip **bent from below**, read from a hundred and seventy meters. **Oryn's lore**: "Big. Under. Comes up. Nobody's seen it whole."
book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:32:- **Lowmarch (129–131):** the fifth honest catalogue, from the landing. **The season line read** (protected); the ledger turned toward him; **no number**; "too small" (protected); the room's "Eleventh." / "Aye." **Teague's term** and "Noted." The healer's single look at Brom's shoulder. **The winter fence** given over ("Ours."). Karis takes the back room and pays without counting (ninety-six). **The inventory** (protected; the audio rule). **The last ferry**: nine pieces sorted aloud; **Hesk's straightedge** with the note (protected); the replies west (protected). **Oryn's letter by carter** the morning after (protected): "Six, by letter." "She'll say when." / "Spring." **The map**: four circles, the bearing, both edges laid along it, **touching the three paced centres for Cael exactly as for Karis**. "The sites were on an alignment. Not random." "Someone made this pattern." Four seconds. **The closing, exact.**
book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:47:The bearing's country; the Hall's water and stone; the fight's moment-to-moment inside the taught rule; the marsh's two days; Teague's manner beside the fire; the walk's last autumn; the crest at dusk; the road home into snow; the inn by lamp; every window.
book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:51:Book 8 Ch1: Lowmarch with the ice coming and the ferry's ropes taken in. Ninety-six in hand. A kit on a table. A map with a line going off its edge. A healer at Thornwater with a route and an arm to release. A captain's spring term. A fourth circle twice the size behind a fence of iron. And a question asked once at a table that nobody answered.
book-07-void-roads/STATE_LEDGER.md:53:- **Seasons:** late summer into the back of autumn, with first snow on the 129th. The mail ferry runs monthly: inbound on about the 60th and the 91st; outbound on the 102nd; the last run on the 130th.
book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:40:- **Teague:** "Spring. Whatever's on that bearing. My crew comes." / "Noted." His crew (four plus an older healer of no Path) winters at Lowmarch. He has given the axe-head hold's long fence (forty, HOLD) to the five for the winter.
book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:43:- **The Quieting, as known:** four sites on one alignment. The Fallow Ring, the Long Stair and the Drowned Hall have been entered. The fourth was paced from outside on the 123rd: **four hundred metres' radius**, ringed by a **cordon of iron stakes numbered thirty-four, with the stroke-and-bar mark, a pace apart**. Not entered, not named, its effect unknown, its central shape a standing grey thing nobody has a word for. "Someone made this pattern." was said once and not answered.
