    13	## 1. Entry state and ending state (binding)
    14	
    15	### Entry (Book 6 close, drafted prose — B6 Ch23–24; Book 7 Ch1 opens on the same ground)
    16	
    17	- **Where/when:** the switchback shelf above an unnamed valley, the first camp beyond the Registry Line. Book 7 dates everything *past the Line*: Book 6's "sixth day" from Ostrand is Book 7's **second day past the Line**.
    18	- **Party: FIVE.** Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln. Book 6's cards counted six. Book 6's prose settled on five ("the sixth" is Seln's empty desk). Six only after Oryn.
    19	- **Cael:** eighteen (turned on the page in B6 Ch14). **Nine confirmed fragments + the Tide-adjacent anomaly** (session nine, B2), uncounted, under the standing words "Still open. Still real. Patience." No injury open (the Crown-yard forearm bruise is a week from gone; the eleven-minute bill was paid on the road east). The Power Log is in Hesk's satchel, about a third of its leaves left.
    20	- **The seal:** Shadow-adjacent is sealed from any witness who could carry it west, because a defector's tradecraft in Cael's hands would confirm the surveillance-era acquisition. It costs from waking and drifts at dusk. The seal holds out here.
    21	- **Companions:** Lira, Wind, Iron R1 formal (Silver bracket declined at full price). Brom, Iron Skin, Copper formal for good, continental Copper champion. Karis, Ember, ranking forfeited, three boxes made into a field archive. Seln, Shadow, Bronze, left the Compact in form, carrying the locked case (the machine's own maintenance records). All uninjured. Lira and Brom have read the log. Karis sees demonstrations, not the log. Seln knows the mechanism since B6 Ch15.
    22	- **Who knows the mechanism:** those five. Nobody else on the continent.
    23	- **Objects:** a cart, a horse, three boxes and Seln's case under one canvas (B6 Ch24; see conflict C1). Two letters, to Hesk and to Vell, written at the shelf and held for the first westbound courier. Daeva's reply already went west from the ford. The registry's printed continental sheet and the Ternhall straightedge are in Karis's middle box.
    24	- **Compact posture:** the file reads *Active non-compliance. Observation priority escalated.* Asset-restriction is *pending jurisdiction*, meaning it executes the hour any of them shows paper west of the Line. The last watcher turned back at the provincial marker. The faceless faction is unnamed and unlocated. Vastin is inside, no longer the Compact's instrument, writing nothing.
    25	- **Quiet ground:** unknown to every one of them. Nobody has heard the words.
    26	- **The last line:** "nothing anywhere was deciding what he was, except him."
    27	
    28	### Ending (Book 7 close, days 129–131 — must match the source and Book 8 Ch1)
    29	
    30	- **Where/when:** Lowmarch in first snow on the 129th day past the Line. The ferry's last run on the 130th. Oryn's letter by carter on the morning of the 131st. Book 8 Ch1 opens on the 131st.
    31	- **Cael:** **nineteen** (turned on the page on the 102nd, at Thornwater). **Ten confirmed fragments.** The tenth is **Tide-adjacent** (Oryn; partial; Iron; self and contact; *Engagement: clinical — non-hostile*), acquired on the 100th. The anomaly is now **a location, not an entry: the still place.** It was read three times. It does not flow and does not change, and everything goes around it. It is not the Quiet and not a fragment. Not touched since a healer said *stop*. Ribs quiet again since the marsh. Calf a closed seam.
    32	- **The rule on the tenth, in Oryn's hand and his:** *ask first, every time.* It was paid once, by not reading Teague.
    33	- **Lira:** left forearm bitten through at the Ring, mended at the line, reopened on the Stair and closed again. **Still slung and under Oryn's order at first snow** ("She'll say when"). Right ankle taped and **never mended in this book.** Carries Oryn's crossbow on its strap (hers from the Hall, Ch21).
    34	- **Brom:** right shoulder bolted on the Stair and mended, reopened in the Hall and mended a second time ("Twice… not three times this season"). Then bound by Teague's healer of no Path and carried guarded. Carries the kit and the middle box.
    35	- **Karis:** holds the field archive: **52 sheets** of copied walls (Ring 11 / Stair 29 / Hall 12); the kit's **field ledger** (given her by Seln on the road home); the carter's map with **four circles and the bearing**; the Ternhall straightedge. She named the Quieting. Her hypothesis stays unentered. She has the inn's back room for the sheets.
    36	- **Seln:** unmarked all book. The case carried, unopened, targeted, kept. Angry once (the Stair's rim: "No faces." and a broken stock).
    37	- **Oryn:** at Thornwater on her route, **three weeks late there** and the route whole. Letter: "Six, by letter." She learned the mechanism on the 100th. She has not heard any theory, because there is none.
    38	- **Who knows the mechanism:** six (Oryn added). Teague, Pike, the holds and the faceless faction do not.
    39	- **Pike's board:** **nine completed lines** under the five names (the last three are the traverse, the Ring and the Stair). The Stair's price column reads *three hundred; taken; not paid*. The **season line** has been read aloud. **No line number entered**: "First time it's been wrong about a crew by being too small." The five names stay **eleventh** on the wall, unchanged.
    40	- **Teague:** "Spring. Whatever's on that bearing. My crew comes." / "Noted." His crew (four plus an older healer of no Path) winters at Lowmarch. He has given the axe-head hold's long fence (forty, HOLD) to the five for the winter.
    41	- **Money:** **ninety-six in hand** (a hundred and two, less six to the inn for the back room). Three hundred entered as taken and never to be paid.
    42	- **Objects:** the kit (case, pacing cord knotted at the fives, stake thirty-two with the stroke-and-bar mark and a bright point, mallet); the ledger; the 52 sheets; the map; **two brass straightedges** (Ternhall's; Hesk's, arrived on the last ferry). Both touch the three paced centres without daylight, **in Cael's hand as in anyone's** (Book 8 Ch1 owns the first hair of error). Also three boxes, Seln's case, one mule (the crew's), and Oryn's crossbow with one bolt left in it.
    43	- **The Quieting, as known:** four sites on one alignment. The Fallow Ring, the Long Stair and the Drowned Hall have been entered. The fourth was paced from outside on the 123rd: **four hundred metres' radius**, ringed by a **cordon of iron stakes numbered thirty-four, with the stroke-and-bar mark, a pace apart**. Not entered, not named, its effect unknown, its central shape a standing grey thing nobody has a word for. "Someone made this pattern." was said once and not answered.
    44	- **The Compact:** knows quiet ground exists and what it does, and which crew walks out of it (a completion report on the Fallow contract; the rim on the Stair saw a practitioner walk out *declaring*). **It does not know that anything works inside.** Asset-restriction is still pending. The nameless second Anchor hand: "the account's getting longer."
    45	- **Letters west on the last ferry:** to Hesk ("Nineteen, past the Line, and there's a roof…") and to Vell ("There's a second ledger on the continent…").
    46	- **Last paragraph:** verbatim (§10, Ch24).
