### F.5 Noticed while re-running (outside §D; touches B2, B3, B9 wording)

**The direction of Iron ranks in the edition.** B5 seeds "the foot of the Iron seeding against its head" and puts "Lira at the foot of the Iron seeding, because she's Rank One" (ch3:17); "a host-house Rank One, advanced at the last sitting … registered after her, and so stood below her" (ch20:231); the top seed at the confluence is a Stone "who had gone up to Rank Eight" (ch21:63); a "retired Iron Rank Nine" is a master of his floor (ch12:63; ch13:237 "from the sixth rank of Iron to the fifth of Bronze, and a retired Rank Nine"). So in the edition **Iron Rank One is Iron's entry rank (the foot) and the numbers rise toward Nine**; the source's ladder "Iron R1 → Silver bracket" (BM:518) assumed the reverse. Nothing in the B6 plan states the reverse outright, but the ladder line, "Lira's internal trial" (§3 item 4) and the B9 definition all invite it. Lira's ladder in the edition is by RATING (her 25–27 is Silver-touched under #38; "The Standard doesn't read certificates", ch6:183) at an advancement evaluation, not up the Iron ranks. Also BM:509's vocabulary "Rank 1–10": B5 shows ranks to Nine; a tenth is unattested.
