    28	- **The Thornwater road (days 41–43), ≈4,000:** the carter at the fire ("Two carts went quiet on it last month"); the stretch at dusk after a wheel cost an hour; positions; the valley's noise; **Lira's hand up at a hole in the noise**; Seln without turning, "Don't declare anything." / "Walk. Same pace."; "I could clear it." / "No." / "I know. I'm saying it so I've said it."; Brom becoming exactly as large as his body and no larger; Karis deciding five times not to take out the notebook; the five items (keeps station at forty meters; makes no sound; tracks the buckle; won't cross the gravel fan; reacts to nothing because they gave it nothing); it stops a hundred meters short of the fence. No blow struck.
