+- **Names and roles:** no B7 plan line calls the waystation keeper “she”; Ephram's letter correctly uses Bracken as “he” (`BOOK_MAP.md:264`; `MOVEMENT-004.md:39`). Jent is not used as the Compact's face; “the annex” and “the house's counsel” are not misapplied. No B7 official instrument presently substitutes *Cael* where the formal registry name *Caelen Hesk-ward* is required; keep OWNER #44 in force if one is added.
+- **Ratings and formats:** no B7 planned formal bout supplies a worked figure or format that contradicts OWNER #38/#39. Do not import source-edition scales if a later scene adds one.
+- **Brom's title:** `BOOK_MAP.md:354` already catches that the Copper Crown was Lira's and directs the edition to Brom's continental Copper title. The adjacent “three years” should simply be omitted if the source beat is rendered, under A3's non-increment convention.
+
+---
+
+## F. Re-run after Book 6 M8–M9 close (required)
+
+This section is the analogue of the model audit's §F. It cannot be completed on 2026-10-11 because Book 6 M8 is being drafted and M9 has not started. Re-run against **surviving prose plus the coordinator-rulings and CLOSED notes**, never the author end-state alone.
+
+### F1. After M8 (edition chapters 48–54) closes
+
+1. Confirm the ruling's exact text and date against the ratified day-201 calendar.
+2. Confirm Brom's finding, whether he signs anything, the Velmere letter's sealed/open state, and his formal standing.
+3. Confirm Lira's advancement-evaluation result and exact standing; do not infer “Silver bracket declined at full price” from the packet.
+4. Confirm Karis's advocate language and what, if anything, has actually been forfeited by M8 close.
+5. Confirm the Blade notice verbatim, tier, acquisition/engagement wording, cost, integration state, and actual chapter:line. Only then promote the fragment count from eight to nine.
+6. Confirm Havel remains at six sheets; Ilsev and Ephram learn nothing prohibited.
+7. Confirm Gault remains evaluator of record and Vastin remains Archmarshal/certifying office.
+
+### F2. After M9 (edition chapters 55–60) closes
+
+1. Confirm the final five, the four filed withdrawals, Seln's form of departure, Ephram staying, and each person's exact standing.
+2. Reconstruct the calendar from day 203 through the academic-year close, Line crossing, and second day past the Line.
+3. Inventory bodies and every object: Hesk satchel and remaining leaves; three boxes and their contents; Seln's case; cart/horse or substitutes; purse; printed sheet; Ternhall straightedge; Velmere letter; Hesk/Vell/Daeva letters.
+4. Confirm the final nine-item inventory, the uncounted anomaly's exact language, Anchor idle, Shadow sealed, and deployment since the Line.
+5. Confirm the exact file-status punctuation and capitalization.
+6. Replace every B7 “B6 Ch23–24” or old source chapter pointer with actual edition chapters 48–60 and the CLOSED ledger blocks.
+7. Grep the closed Book 6 prose for any final use of a season/month/English weekday, metric unit, or incremented “four years” wording before treating the seam as clean.
+
+---
+
+## G. Proposed order of amendments
+
+1. **Gate the seam:** mark Book 7 §1, the entry ledger, and M1's entry paragraph PENDING B6 M8–M9; replace all source-Ch23–24 drafting directions (A1).
+2. **Apply edition-wide language defaults:** remove named seasons and metric units, including protected B7 wording and downstream Book 8 callbacks; preserve weather and feet/yards/paces/cords (A2).
+3. **Fix M1's canon lesson:** replace the four-year count with “since his Kindling”; add Storm's air/body and ten/ten/twelve bill; replace the Anchor row with its full B6 history and 10/12/14-ft perception (A3–A5).
+4. **Repair capability logic before issuing later packets:** enforce the Anchor range, carry the Gold read's medium choice, and restage Shadow's M5 use so Oryn cannot see or attribute it (B1–B3).
+5. **Repair the Kindling/Quiet language:** separate Arbiter, plate, Path and fragments; make the B7 disclosure a retelling to Oryn, not a new revelation; revise the protected logs and close (B4, B7).
+6. **Repair Seln continuity:** edition M6/ch37 citation, “You kept my file too,” twice-more count two, and twelve-year case history (B5–B6).
+7. **Correct source citations and light texture:** edition acquisition chapters, remove Seln's unsupported age, and hold the exact file-status form pending M9 (C1–C3).
+8. **After B6 M8 closes, execute F1** and promote only confirmed M8 outcomes (D1–D2, D5).
+9. **After B6 M9 closes, execute F2** and rebuild the complete physical/calendar/document seam from the surviving prose (D3–D5).
+10. **Only then release Book 7 Movement 1 for drafting**, with every entry fact sourced to the edition's Book 6 rather than the pre-edition source.

