+# Book 7 plan vs edition Book 6 canon — reconciliation audit
+
+> Built by Sol (continuity audit seat, fresh context) — 2026-10-11
+> Scope: `book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md`, `STATE_LEDGER.md` (entry), and `packets/MOVEMENT-001.md` … `MOVEMENT-008.md`, all written before the edition's Book 6 existed, checked against `book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md` (coordinator-rulings blocks and CLOSED notes through Movement 7), `BOOK_MAP.md` (§1, §8, §9, §11), the Book 6 M8 and M9 packets (PLAN only), OWNER-DECISIONS #35–#45, and spot-checks of the edition Book 6 manuscript through chapter 47. Where the Book 7 plan reaches farther back, the closed Book 4–5 ledgers, director-cut notices, and acquisition chapters were checked.
+>
+> Read-only audit. No plan file was edited. Line numbers are as of this date. Bede, Maud, Gwen and Abbot are owner-pending placeholders, not findings.
+
+## Severity key
+
+- **BLOCKS M1** — Movement 1 drafted to the current packet/map/ledger would contradict closed Book 6 (or earlier edition canon), or the packet sends the author to superseded source facts. Amend before the M1 author session.
+- **Affects later movement** — the contradiction lands in M2–M8; amend before that packet is issued.
+- **Cosmetic** — a pointer, unsupported texture detail, capitalization, or one-line terminology repair.
+- **PENDING B6 M8–M9** — Book 7 currently assumes an outcome from Book 6 chapters 48–60 that is only planned. Do not promote it to canon until the applicable Book 6 coordinator block is CLOSED.
+
+Book 6 is closed only through chapter 47 / Movement 7 (`book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:990`). The Book 6 M8 and M9 packets explicitly remain plans; their coordinator notes are at `packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:9` and `packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:9`. Accordingly, no M8/M9 outcome is treated as canon below.
+
+---
+
+## A. BLOCKS M1 (5 findings)
+
+### A1. The seam points to source Book 6 chapters, and calls an unfinished close “drafted prose”
+
+- **B7 says:** `BOOK_MAP.md:7` sends the seam read to “Book 6 Ch23–24”; `:15` labels the Book 6 close “drafted prose — B6 Ch23–24”; `STATE_LEDGER.md:3` says its entry was built from “the Book 6 close as drafted (B6 Ch23–24)”; `packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:13` tells the author to read Book 6 `chapter-23.md`, `chapter-24.md`.
+- **B6 canon:** the edition is closed only through chapter 47 (`STATE_LEDGER.md:990`). M8 is planned for edition chapters 48–54 (`packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:1–9`); M9 is planned for chapters 55–60 (`packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:1–9`). The M7 coordinator block fixes the calendar but explicitly leaves the departure to M8/M9 (`STATE_LEDGER.md:994–1025`).
+- **Why it matters:** the source Ch23–24 contain facts the edition changed, while the actual edition hand-off does not yet exist. M1's entry paragraph currently gives unearned authority to five travellers, the cart and horse, nine fragments, letters, resignations, and the second-day camp.
+- **Severity:** **BLOCKS M1** (process and entry state), with the underlying facts **PENDING B6 M8–M9**.
+- **Amend:** replace every “B6 Ch23–24” seam instruction with: “edition Book 6 `STATE_LEDGER.md`, AFTER MOVEMENT 7 coordinator rulings first; then the CLOSED AFTER MOVEMENT 8/9 blocks and surviving edition chapters 48–60 when they exist.” Until then, label §1 and the entry ledger **PROVISIONAL — PENDING B6 M8–M9**, not “drafted prose.” Keep the old source chapters events-only and list every edition override in M1 rather than sending the author to them as canon.
+
+### A2. Season names and metres violate the edition's standing defaults
+
+- **B7 says, in M1:** `packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:28` uses “forty meters” and “a hundred meters”; `:49` uses “autumn road.” The protected M1 log at `BOOK_MAP.md:272` says “Season's open,” and the M1 packet requires it exact (`MOVEMENT-001.md:29`, `:36`).
+- **The same problem continues:** `BOOK_MAP.md:40`, `:43`, `:59`, `:165`, `:206`, `:240`, `:269`, `:284`, `:307`, `:317`, `:321`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:53`; `MOVEMENT-002.md:16`, `:37`; `MOVEMENT-004.md:28`, `:47`; `MOVEMENT-005.md:22–23`, `:44`; `MOVEMENT-006.md:45`; `MOVEMENT-007.md:16`, `:28–29`; `MOVEMENT-008.md:22–23`, `:32`, `:47`, `:51`. These include *spring*, *autumn*, *winter*, and metric distances. (`MOVEMENT-008.md:23` also has a literal water spring; that one is not a season use.)
+- **B6 canon:** “Season-blind (#42); feet and yards” (`book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:139`); the rule is repeated at `:1040`. OWNER #42 requires no season or month names (`OWNER-DECISIONS.md:121–126`). Closed Book 5 also carries season-blind as a default (`book-05-the-silver-standard/DIRECTOR_CUT_READY.md:20`).
+- **Severity:** **BLOCKS M1** at `MOVEMENT-001.md:28–29`, `:49` and the protected M1 lines; **Affects later movement** everywhere else.
+- **Amend:** convert all metric distances to feet/yards or the plan's already established paces/strides/cords. Replace named seasons with weather, road, term, route, or elapsed-day wording. Specific protected-line defaults: “Year's open” for `BOOK_MAP.md:272`; “cold-road” or simply “east road” for *autumn road*; “the cold-road fence” for *winter fence*; “next term” or a day-relative appointment for Teague's *Spring*. Mark downstream Book 8 quotations for its own reconciliation; Book 8's protection does not overrule OWNER #42 for this edition.
+
+### A3. M1 increments the forbidden year count, including in protected text
+
+- **B7 says:** `packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:21` makes “four years of not-using” the learned competence; the protected first-pole log at `BOOK_MAP.md:273` says “I've spent four years being the case.”
+- **B6 canon:** the Book 6 entry ledger already replaces “four years” with “his time since his Kindling” (`book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:28`). Book 5's governing non-increment rule is recorded at `book-05-the-silver-standard/STATE_LEDGER.md:122`; the Book 6 reconciliation applied the same rule. The M9 packet also carries the required closing form, “for the first time since his Kindling” (`book-06-the-compacts-hand/packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:47`, plan). OWNER #18's convention is “since his Kindling,” not an incremented number.
+- **Severity:** **BLOCKS M1**.
+- **Amend:** `MOVEMENT-001.md:21` → “the discipline of not using into the only competence that pays.” In the protected pole, replace “I've spent four years being the case” with “Since my Kindling I've been the case the instruments couldn't parse.” Record this as a canon amendment to protected wording, not an author variance.
+
+### A4. M1's taught inventory omits Book 6's binding Storm limits
+
+- **B7 says:** the entry ledger gives Storm only “short range,” “heaviest,” and “resettles” (`STATE_LEDGER.md:75`); M1 names only “Storm sitting heavy” (`packets/MOVEMENT-001.md:27`); the progression table says merely that Storm is heaviest and resettles (`BOOK_MAP.md:191`).
+- **B6 canon:** at Gold weight the read takes **air or body, not both** (`STATE_LEDGER.md:145`; manuscript `chapter-04.md:175`). Each of the first three lanes is billed from laying: **ten / ten / twelve**, clean at eleven / eleven / thirteen (`STATE_LEDGER.md:449`). The after-effect is the right thing answering late, a **bill, not flag** (`chapter-04.md:193–209`).
+- **Severity:** **BLOCKS M1**, because M1 is the book's explicit inventory lesson (`BOOK_MAP.md:180`; `MOVEMENT-001.md:11`, `:27`).
+- **Amend:** expand the Storm row and M1 inventory note to: “short-range lane; at Gold the read is air or body; lane bill ten/ten/twelve, clean eleven/eleven/thirteen; after-effect is everything answering a beat late — bill, not flag; untested past three.” Keep resettling as an additional idle/integration fact, not the capability's whole cost.
+
+### A5. M1's taught Anchor entry state omits two uses and sends the author to the wrong edition chapter
+
+- **B7 says:** `STATE_LEDGER.md:76` cites “B6 Ch13” and reduces Anchor to fixed-point binding, lattice perception, doorway want, and release; M1 teaches “Anchor wanting every doorway since the Ostrand road” (`MOVEMENT-001.md:27`).
+- **B6 canon:** Anchor is fixed points, lines, and a cage; it was used **once on purpose** to unbind the cage and **once uncommanded** to hold the doorway for twelve seconds (`STATE_LEDGER.md:793`). The cage and release are on the edition page at `manuscript/chapter-31.md:191–231`; the uncommanded doorway is in `chapter-33.md:113–151`. Its perception is sure to about ten feet, faint at twelve, nothing at fourteen (`STATE_LEDGER.md:906`; `chapter-38.md:341–345`).
+- **Severity:** **BLOCKS M1** for the entry inventory and source direction; the later distance contradiction is B1.
+- **Amend:** rewrite the entry row to cite edition B6 ch31/ch33/ch38 and state: “fixed points; lines; cage; purposeful unbinding once; uncommanded twelve-second doorway once; perception sure ~10 ft, faint 12, none 14; reach/rate/price otherwise unknown.” M1 may summarize those known facts but must not make the doorway want the whole capability.
+
+---
+
+## B. Affects later movement (7 findings)
+
+### B1. Anchor is repeatedly given a ten-metre perception range
+
+- **B7 says:** `packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:29` twice makes Anchor perception operate at “ten meters”; `BOOK_MAP.md:189` does not preserve the numeric perception cap. M5 also has Anchor seeing Karis's points before they light (`MOVEMENT-005.md:22`) without fixing Cael inside the known range.
+- **B6 canon:** sure to about **10 ft**, faint at 12 ft, nothing at 14 ft; what it can *reach* remains unmeasured (`STATE_LEDGER.md:906`; `chapter-38.md:341–345`).
+- **Severity:** **Affects later movement** (M5 and M7).
+- **Amend:** change both M7 “ten meters” uses to **ten feet**. Stage Cael within ten feet of any M5 point he perceives. Do not infer reach from perception, and leave reach/rate/price blank except for the already-canonical unbinding and uncommanded doorway.
+
+### B2. The first planned Shadow use is visible to Oryn before she joins the trusted knowledge circle
+
+- **B7 says:** Shadow is first used at the Ring, “circle and Oryn only” (`BOOK_MAP.md:188`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:74`; `packets/MOVEMENT-005.md:22`, `:31`). Oryn does not learn the mechanism until M6 (`MOVEMENT-005.md:35`; `MOVEMENT-006.md:22`).
+- **B6 canon:** “While its use can be seen by anyone who could carry the seeing west, it stays sealed” (`STATE_LEDGER.md:904`; `manuscript/chapter-37.md:202`). The debt is closed but the seal is kept on Seln's terms (`chapter-37.md:208`).
+- **Why it matters:** “circle and Oryn only” does not satisfy the term. Oryn is still an outsider when the use occurs, and the current plan gives her line of sight to exactly the tradecraft the seal protects.
+- **Severity:** **Affects later movement** (M5).
+- **Amend:** restage the Ring use so Oryn cannot see or attribute it: blocked sightline, attention fixed on Lira/Karis, and no observable discontinuity she can carry west. State in the packet that “circle” here means only the already-informed B6 circle. The M6 telling does not automatically waive Seln's term; if the use moves later, the plan must still establish that every observer either cannot see/attribute it or cannot carry the seeing west.
+
+### B3. The Gold read's air-or-body choice is absent from every B7 use
+
+- **B7 says:** `STATE_LEDGER.md:71` gives only range, mass/vector, and price; `BOOK_MAP.md:187` sends the read across the line, under his soles, and under water; M5 makes it run “under his soles the whole retreat” (`MOVEMENT-005.md:22`).
+- **B6 canon:** at Gold weight the read takes **air or body**, not both; lane first means giving up the body read (`STATE_LEDGER.md:145`; `manuscript/chapter-04.md:175`).
+- **Severity:** **Affects later movement** (M4, M5, M7, M8).
+- **Amend:** add the air/body choice to `STATE_LEDGER.md:71` and `BOOK_MAP.md:187`. In every action beat, specify which medium he is reading. Where Storm lays a lane, state that the read is in the air and unavailable for body/ground until relinquished; never narrate both simultaneously.
+
+### B4. The Kindling mechanics are both mis-timed and treated as newly discoverable
+
+- **B7 says:** the Arbiter is “Dark since eleven seconds at fourteen” (`BOOK_MAP.md:194`). The Quiet logs say “Mine didn't” stop at the line (`:279–280`), “Mine has been asleep since I was fourteen” (`:281`), and “I've known [it isn't a Path] since I was fourteen” (`:282`). M6's telling begins “fourteen, eleven seconds, a training floor, the count” and says nobody has attached a condition to the mechanism before (`packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:22`).
+- **B6 canon:** Kindling is the person's own Arbiter waking and a brass plate lighting; station records hold the keeper's frame reading and margin; the corrections function failed safe; the bracketed word was written over the old name (`STATE_LEDGER.md:903`). The Arbiter wakes before the late plate; the plate lights at eleven seconds (`manuscript/chapter-36.md:117`; `chapter-37.md:15`), the failed-safe reading is already on the page (`chapter-39.md:59–63`), and the bracketed word is identified as written over the old name (`chapter-39.md:127–129`).
+- **Why it matters:** an Arbiter already dark cannot be observed “not stopping” at the Quiet line. The B7 plan also risks re-revealing to the reader and the five what B6 M6 already established; only Oryn is new to it.
+- **Severity:** **Affects later movement** (M4–M6).
+- **Amend:** `BOOK_MAP.md:194` → “Own Arbiter woke at Kindling, then went dark after the failed-safe word; station plate lit eleven seconds late.” Rewrite `:279–282` so Cael records only the observable fact: “mine was dark before and after; the line changed nothing I could feel; my fragments still worked.” Do not call the dark Arbiter “awake.” In M6, frame the scene as **the B6-established mechanism retold to Oryn**, with Lira/Brom/Karis/Seln already knowing; her new condition applies to Tide use, not to the pre-existing mechanism.
+
+### B5. Seln's knowledge timing and “twice more” limit are not carried into the B7 entry state
+
+- **B7 says:** Seln knows “since B6 Ch15” (`BOOK_MAP.md:21`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:95`) and the B7 entry records neither his exact recognition nor the remaining tell-count.
+- **B6 canon:** Seln knows as of edition B6 M6: Cael tells the mechanism end to end with the circle present; Seln says “You kept my file too, then”; and “twice more” stands at **two** (`STATE_LEDGER.md:902`, `:1033`, `:1051`; manuscript `chapter-37.md:99–103`, `:182`).
+- **Severity:** **Affects later movement**, principally M6's disclosure scene and every Seln window.
+- **Amend:** replace “since B6 Ch15” with “since edition B6 M6 / ch37.” Add to the entry knowledge row: “recognized that Cael kept his file; exact line already spent; mechanism may be told to him twice more, count still two at B6 M7 close.” Ensure no B7 recap to Seln consumes a telling accidentally.
+
+### B6. Seln's case history is shortened from twelve years to six
+
+- **B7 says:** Seln's M7 window is “six years carrying a case” (`BOOK_MAP.md:145`; `packets/MOVEMENT-007.md:9`), and his council line says “Six years I've wanted a face” (`MOVEMENT-007.md:25`; protected at `BOOK_MAP.md:314`).
+- **B6 canon:** “I have kept the case **twelve years**” (`manuscript/chapter-37.md:103`); Cael immediately retains that as “The case had been kept twelve years” (`:254`).
+- **Severity:** **Affects later movement** (M7).
+- **Amend:** use “twelve years carrying the case” where the case history is meant. If “wanted a face” begins at a later suppression event, the plan must identify that distinct trigger; otherwise change the protected line to “Twelve years I've wanted a face” or remove the numeral (“All these years…”).
+
