+
+- **B7 says:** “every Path in the party stops at except his” (`MOVEMENT-004.md:20`); “Everyone's Path dies at the line and mine didn't” (`BOOK_MAP.md:280`); the exact close repeats “every Path in the party had stopped at a line and his had not” (`BOOK_MAP.md:321`).
+- **B6 canon:** the corrected Kindling explanation is that Cael's Arbiter failed safe and went dark; Book 6 never establishes a surviving Cael Path. The closed state is eight fragments plus an uncounted anomaly, with Anchor and Shadow idle/sealed (`STATE_LEDGER.md:1075–1076`).
+- **Severity:** **Affects later movement** (M4–M8).
+- **Amend:** distinguish Arbiter, Path, and fragments throughout: “five live Arbiters stopped; Cael's was dark before and after; his fragments continued to answer.” The final paragraph should say “every live Arbiter in the party stopped at a line; his fragments did not.” Do not let Cael or the narration call those fragments “his Path.”
+
+---
+
+## C. Cosmetic and sourcing corrections (3 findings)
+
+### C1. Three acquisition/source citations point to source-edition chapter numbers
+
+- **B7 says:** Shadow from “B4 Ch13,” Storm from “B5 Ch21,” Anchor from “B6 Ch13” (`STATE_LEDGER.md:74–76`).
+- **Edition canon:** Shadow's acquisition notice is edition B4 `manuscript/chapter-34.md:140–141` (also `book-04-copper-crown/STATE_LEDGER.md:444`, `:488`); Storm's notice is edition B5 `manuscript/chapter-56.md:194–195`; Anchor's capability is established across edition B6 ch31/ch33/ch38 (`book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:793`, `:906`).
