+- **B6 plan only:** the ruling, Brom's finding, Karis's departure cost, and drafted resignations are M8 beats (`packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:22–35`); filing/forfeiture and walk-out are M9 beats (`packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:22–28`).
+- **Severity:** **PENDING B6 M8–M9**.
+- **Amend:** mark each standing individually pending. After M8 closes, inherit the actual panel/evaluation/ruling language; after M9 closes, inherit the filed (not merely drafted) withdrawal/forfeiture state. Preserve B6 M7 body canon meanwhile: Lira's right ankle sound, left-arm carry habit only (`STATE_LEDGER.md:1044`); Brom's left shoulder working but under review (`:1045`, `:1079`).
+
+### D3. The five-person departure, Ephram's absence, objects, letters and injury-free shelf are all planned, not closed
+
+- **B7 assumes:** five travellers and “second day past the Line” (`BOOK_MAP.md:17–18`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:11`; `MOVEMENT-001.md:17`); cart, horse, three boxes, case and letters (`BOOK_MAP.md:23`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:116–122`); Ephram stayed (`STATE_LEDGER.md:151`); everyone is uninjured (`BOOK_MAP.md:19`, `:21`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:60`, `:92–95`).
+- **Closed B6 state:** at M7, the party is still at Halcenvane; Karis's three boxes are on the deposit shelf, Brom's two under his bed, the case on Karis's shelf, and the letters/route departure have not occurred (`STATE_LEDGER.md:1064–1072`).
+- **B6 plan only:** five cross, Ephram stays, letters are held, the boxes/case leave, and the camp ends on the second day past the Line (`packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:22–39`). The cart/horse explanation is explicitly left to the M9 author (`:43`).
+- **Severity:** **PENDING B6 M8–M9**.
+- **Amend:** keep a provisional seam checklist rather than declarative entry canon: final five; bodies; open injuries; exact containers and owners; cart/horse acquisition; purse; letters held/sent; Ephram; satchel/log; case custody. Populate it from M9's surviving prose and CLOSED ledger, then amend M1's first paragraph to match exactly.
+
+### D4. The B6→B7 calendar seam is only partly ratified
+
+- **B7 assumes:** “Book 6's sixth day from Ostrand is Book 7's second day past the Line” (`BOOK_MAP.md:17`), and the ledger begins on that day (`STATE_LEDGER.md:11`).
+- **Closed B6 canon:** ruling day 201; M8 council/bout preferably day 202; M9 entry day 203; academic year closes day 207; the Line is crossed after day 207 (`STATE_LEDGER.md:994–1025`).
+- **B6 plan only:** M9 ends on the second day past the Line (`packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:38`, `:47`). The actual count of road days and the Line crossing are not yet on the page.
+- **Severity:** **PENDING B6 M8–M9**.
+- **Amend:** retain the B7 relative clock (“second day past the Line”) provisionally, but delete “Book 6's sixth day from Ostrand” until M9 prose supplies that exact count. On re-run, map every M9 road day from day 203 through the crossing and prove that the academic year has already closed.
+
+### D5. Several named documents and closing facts cannot yet be source material for B7
+
+- **B7 assumes:** Gault's last note beside the Fallow copy (`MOVEMENT-006.md:25`); the closing file status (`BOOK_MAP.md:24`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:86`); the Power Log, letters, printed sheet and straightedge in their B7 carriers (`BOOK_MAP.md:19`, `:23`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:116–120`); Vastin “inside, no longer the Compact's instrument, writing nothing” (`BOOK_MAP.md:24`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:112`, `:163`).
+- **Closed B6 state:** Gault remains evaluator of record (the ledger distinguishes him from Vastin at `STATE_LEDGER.md:1027`; Gault's notes are produced at `:1031`); Vastin has declined certification and writes nothing, but remains inside (`:1056`). Havel has exactly six sheets (`:1032`, `:1057`, `:1072`). The Velmere letter is still sealed (`:1028`).
+- **B6 plan only:** Gault's last note, the final file line, Vastin's end-state, the field archive's departure, and the letters' shelf state are M8/M9 beats (`packets/MOVEMENT-008.md:22–31`; `MOVEMENT-009.md:22–32`).
+- **Severity:** **PENDING B6 M8–M9**.
+- **Amend:** after closure, source each document to the actual edition chapter and copy exact wording only where protected. Do not relabel Vastin evaluator of record; Gault remains that officer. Confirm Havel stops at six, Brom's Velmere letter disposition, Karis's advocate/forfeiture chain, and the final custody of every box, case, log and letter.
+
+---
+
+## E. Checked and presently consistent (no amendment)
+
+- **Anomaly count:** B7 keeps the Tide-adjacent anomaly uncounted (`STATE_LEDGER.md:78`, `:80`), matching B6's “still place uncounted” (`book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:1075`). Its later conversion into a felt location remains B7's own planned development.
+- **Shadow's governing words:** the B7 entry correctly says the seal is from witnesses who can carry the seeing west (`BOOK_MAP.md:20`; `STATE_LEDGER.md:74`). B2 concerns the staging of the first use, not the definition.
+- **Seln knows:** B7 does not preserve the older “Seln is not told” error. Only the timing/citation and “twice more” state need the B5 finding's correction.
+- **Lira's carried injury:** B7 enters her uninjured, compatible with B6 M7's sound right ankle and left-arm habit only (`B6 STATE_LEDGER.md:1044`). Her Silver outcome remains pending M8.
+- **Brom's body and review:** B7 enters him uninjured, compatible with the M7 body row (`B6 STATE_LEDGER.md:1045`); the formal standing remains pending M8.
+- **Karis:** the B7 plan does not displace her B6 advocate entry. The forfeiture outcome remains pending M8/M9.
+- **Ephram, Havel, Gault, Vastin:** no B7 line turns Ephram into a traveller; Havel is not given a seventh sheet; Gault and Vastin are not explicitly conflated; Vastin's protected window correctly says “forty years” and gives no age (`BOOK_MAP.md:260`).
+- **Names and roles:** no B7 plan line calls the waystation keeper “she”; Ephram's letter correctly uses Bracken as “he” (`BOOK_MAP.md:264`; `MOVEMENT-004.md:39`). Jent is not used as the Compact's face; “the annex” and “the house's counsel” are not misapplied. No B7 official instrument presently substitutes *Cael* where the formal registry name *Caelen Hesk-ward* is required; keep OWNER #44 in force if one is added.
+- **Renewals:** the B7 plan does not restate or increment the enrollment-renewal count. If it is added later, the governing Book 6 form is “two renewals on paper” (`book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:139`; OWNER #43), apart from the still-owner-pending protected pole.
+- **Ratings and formats:** no B7 planned formal bout supplies a worked figure or format that contradicts OWNER #38/#39. Do not import source-edition scales if a later scene adds one.
+- **Brom's title:** `BOOK_MAP.md:354` already catches that the Copper Crown was Lira's and directs the edition to Brom's continental Copper title. The adjacent “three years” should simply be omitted if the source beat is rendered, under A3's non-increment convention.
+
+---
+
+## F. Re-run after Book 6 M8–M9 close (required)
+
+This section is the analogue of the model audit's §F. It cannot be completed on 2026-10-11 because Book 6 M8 is being drafted and M9 has not started. Re-run against **surviving prose plus the coordinator-rulings and CLOSED notes**, never the author end-state alone.
+
+### F1. After M8 (edition chapters 48–54) closes
+
+1. Confirm the ruling's exact text and date against the ratified day-201 calendar.
+2. Confirm Brom's finding, whether he signs anything, the Velmere letter's sealed/open state, and his formal standing.
+3. Confirm Lira's advancement-evaluation result and exact standing; do not infer “Silver bracket declined at full price” from the packet.
+4. Confirm Karis's advocate language and what, if anything, has actually been forfeited by M8 close.
+5. Confirm the Blade notice verbatim, tier, acquisition/engagement wording, cost, integration state, and actual chapter:line. Only then promote the fragment count from eight to nine.
+6. Confirm Havel remains at six sheets; Ilsev and Ephram learn nothing prohibited.
